{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680339242,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db47c0ee0019B3RdzXj6ykCwj","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db47b67d0017CHtsm2UkIbXzK","type":"tool","id":"call_6e219f3f215e40e6bf72ea86","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-confirm-4b lineage\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking the confirming round of review pass four for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\nversion: 1.11.14.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-confirm-4b lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\niteration before any review action.\n\n### Ownership\n\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nConfirming round of review pass four of\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` in the\n`scorer-attach` area, over the fix commit range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\n\nScope: the `scorer-attach` area rows of `review/review-scope-4b.txt` — `command-attach.ts`,\n`score-command-transcripts.mjs`, the four matching tests, and the shared docs that describe\nthem (`README.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`,\n`feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`). The `accuracy-runner` rows\n(`codex.mjs`, `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, their tests and the doctor\npresentation asset) belong to the sibling lineage and are read here only as context.\n\nThis round confirms the fixes for the findings in `review/verify-4/report.md` and looks for\ndefects those fixes added. A finding the report rejects or records as an accepted limit is not\nre-raised without a new input that breaks it.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — refusal/or-list suppression, is-the question, shell-read start, heredoc close, run-log `offeredAs`\n- [ ] D2 Security — holdout hygiene in the scorer and live capture, guard reach\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — docs against code, spec/checklist claims, feature-catalog claims\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — test pinning, dead fields, naming, follow-on change cost\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The accuracy-runner harness and session readers are the sibling lineage's code scope; this\n  lineage checks only that its own scoring surface agrees with them.\n- Hook, plugin, render and doctor-command code is outside both scope rows.\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 3; the terminal record must carry `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [pending] | - | - | - |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:saturated-dimensions -->\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:saturated-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- SA4-P1-002 confirmation, refusal over an or-list: pending iteration 1.\n- R4-P2-002 (first-row lead): rejected by `verify-4/report.md`; not re-opened without a new input.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the refusal/or-list and is-the question suppression in `command-attach.ts`\n- Reason: it is the only confirmed P1 fix in this round, and its guard reach decides whether a\n  mutating command can still start from a refusal.\n- Required evidence: the post-fix code path plus a concrete input per branch.\n- Recovery note: none.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (refusal and question suppression, heredoc\n  scan, shell-read start), `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n  (`readDocument`, `offeredAs`, holdout guard), `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`,\n  `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n- Behavior claims: a refusal over an or-list carries no command; an is-the question carries no\n  command; a request over a list keeps its command; both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`; a\n  shell read of a command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place `sed`, a\n  redirect and a heredoc line do not; a heredoc end word with `-` or `.` closes correctly; the\n  Codex reader opens the resolved file; the holdout guard reads the live capture; docs agree\n  with code.\n- Conventions: P0/P1/P2 only; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete `Case:`; the\n  five fix-completeness lines are required per finding.\n- Risks: the `verify-4` report rejected three findings; re-raising them needs a new input. The\n  scorer keeps stored baselines, so a doc claim and a stored number can disagree silently.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no playbook in scope |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| [pending] | - | - | - | - |\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 3\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-attach-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-14T19:16:00Z\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-confirm-4b lineage\\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking the confirming round of review pass four for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\\nversion: 1.11.14.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-confirm-4b lineage\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\\niteration before any review action.\\n\\n### Ownership\\n\\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nConfirming round of review pass four of\\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` in the\\n`scorer-attach` area, over the fix commit range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\\n\\nScope: the `scorer-attach` area rows of `review/review-scope-4b.txt` — `command-attach.ts`,\\n`score-command-transcripts.mjs`, the four matching tests, and the shared docs that describe\\nthem (`README.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`,\\n`feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`). The `accuracy-runner` rows\\n(`codex.mjs`, `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, their tests and the doctor\\npresentation asset) belong to the sibling lineage and are read here only as context.\\n\\nThis round confirms the fixes for the findings in `review/verify-4/report.md` and looks for\\ndefects those fixes added. A finding the report rejects or records as an accepted limit is not\\nre-raised without a new input that breaks it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness — refusal/or-list suppression, is-the question, shell-read start, heredoc close, run-log `offeredAs`\\n- [ ] D2 Security — holdout hygiene in the scorer and live capture, guard reach\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability — docs against code, spec/checklist claims, feature-catalog claims\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability — test pinning, dead fields, naming, follow-on change cost\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- The accuracy-runner harness and session readers are the sibling lineage's code scope; this\\n  lineage checks only that its own scoring surface agrees with them.\\n- Hook, plugin, render and doctor-command code is outside both scope rows.\\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold.\\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 3; the terminal record must carry `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| [pending] | - | - | - |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:saturated-dimensions -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:saturated-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- SA4-P1-002 confirmation, refusal over an or-list: pending iteration 1.\\n- R4-P2-002 (first-row lead): rejected by `verify-4/report.md`; not re-opened without a new input.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: the refusal/or-list and is-the question suppression in `command-attach.ts`\\n- Reason: it is the only confirmed P1 fix in this round, and its guard reach decides whether a\\n  mutating command can still start from a refusal.\\n- Required evidence: the post-fix code path plus a concrete input per branch.\\n- Recovery note: none.\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (refusal and question suppression, heredoc\\n  scan, shell-read start), `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\\n  (`readDocument`, `offeredAs`, holdout guard), `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`,\\n  `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\\n- Behavior claims: a refusal over an or-list carries no command; an is-the question carries no\\n  command; a request over a list keeps its command; both run-log writers keep `offeredAs`; a\\n  shell read of a command document counts as a start while a search, an in-place `sed`, a\\n  redirect and a heredoc line do not; a heredoc end word with `-` or `.` closes correctly; the\\n  Codex reader opens the resolved file; the holdout guard reads the live capture; docs agree\\n  with code.\\n- Conventions: P0/P1/P2 only; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete `Case:`; the\\n  five fix-completeness lines are required per finding.\\n- Risks: the `verify-4` report rejected three findings; re-raising them needs a new input. The\\n  scorer keeps stored baselines, so a doc claim and a stored number can disagree silently.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no playbook in scope |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| [pending] | - | - | - | - |\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:files-under-review -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 3\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-attach-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: spec-folder\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-14T19:16:00Z\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-boundaries -->\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680275182,"end":1794680339242}}}}
