   const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:643:      const result = await backfillRunLog({ inPath, outPath: inPath, promptFor: () => 'prompt' });\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1473:      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1475:      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1497: *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offeredAsPartner: boolean,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1545:    offeredAsPartner: offer.partner,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1622:    offeredAsPartner: 0,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1681:    offeredAsPartner: tally.offeredAsPartner,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1771:  if (result.offeredAsPartner) tally.offeredAsPartner += 1;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1924:          + ` offered as partner ${block.offeredAsPartner},`\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:56:import { backfillRunLog, briefDelivered, codexHookApproval, promptSessionId, replayOffer } from './command-offer.mjs';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:816: *   offeredAs?: 'head' | 'partner' | null }} offer - The replayed offer.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:818: *   offeredAs: 'head' | 'partner' | null }} The offer fields a line records.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:824:    offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1262:  const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:69:- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:124:| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:188:The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:53:  return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null, offerError };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:63: * `offeredAs` records whether the match sat before `vs` as the head or after\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:68: *   offeredAs: 'head' | 'partner' | null }}\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:74:    return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:80:    offeredAs: text.slice(0, match.index).includes(' vs ') ? 'partner' : 'head',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:97: *   offeredAs: 'head' | 'partner' | null, offerError: string | null }}\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:414:export async function backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:496:        offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:116:        offeredAs: 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:119:    ).toEqual({ offeredCommand: '/create:readme', offeredPolicy: 'start', offeredAs: 'partner' });\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:125:    ).toEqual({ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null });\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:845:  readonly offeredAs?: 'head' | 'partner' | null;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1219:        tune: { runs: 2, scored: 2, offered: 1, startedOfOffered: 1, offerFieldAbsent: 0, offeredAsPartner: 0 },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1236:          offeredAs: 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1244:          offeredAs: 'head',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1250:      claude: { tune: { runs: 2, scored: 2, offered: 1, offeredAsPartner: 1 } },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:24:  backfillRunLog,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:78:      offeredAs: 'head',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:86:      offeredAs: 'head',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:94:      offeredAs: null,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:102:      offeredAs: 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:110:      offeredAs: 'head',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:156:        offeredAs: null,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:305:describe('backfillRunLog', () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:318:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:366:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:376:              offeredAs: 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:387:      expect(written[0].offeredAs).toBe('partner');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:388:      expect(written[1].offeredAs).toBeNull();\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:410:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:450:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:498:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:548:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:581:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:612:      const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:643:      const result = await backfillRunLog({ inPath, outPath: inPath, promptFor: () => 'prompt' });\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1473:      && line.offeredAs !== 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1475:      && line.offeredAs === 'partner',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1497: *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offeredAsPartner: boolean,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1545:    offeredAsPartner: offer.partner,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1622:    offeredAsPartner: 0,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1681:    offeredAsPartner: tally.offeredAsPartner,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1771:  if (result.offeredAsPartner) tally.offeredAsPartner += 1;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1924:          + ` offered as partner ${block.offeredAsPartner},`\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:56:import { backfillRunLog, briefDelivered, codexHookApproval, promptSessionId, replayOffer } from './command-offer.mjs';\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:816: *   offeredAs?: 'head' | 'partner' | null }} offer - The replayed offer.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:818: *   offeredAs: 'head' | 'partner' | null }} The offer fields a line records.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:824:    offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1262:  const result = await backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:69:- `offeredAs` says where that command sat in the head: `head`, `partner` when it followed `vs` on an ambiguous head, or `null` when the head named none.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:123:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows `--summary` to one row and is a usage error with `--runtime`. `--json` prints machine-readable output. `--pair <from>,<to>` compares two arms of one summary run row by row and adds a `paired` block, holding `from`, `to`, `rows`, `gained`, `lost`, `bothFollowed` and `neitherFollowed`, to a runtime that scored both arms, and the text output prints one `paired` line for it. `--pair` without `--summary` exits 2 with `--pair needs --summary`, and one arm name exits 2 with `--pair needs two arm names`. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, `armIncomplete`, `byPolicy` and `workflow`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. The `workflow` block sorts each run into `command`, `skill`, `improvised`, `none` or `noOwner` and prints `share` as the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before their first write, out of every run that acted. It shows a workflow was loaded, not that each step was followed. The block also carries `noneActed`, the `none` runs that read a file or ran a shell step, and `loadRate`, the runs that loaded the command's or the owning skill's workflow out of every scored run with an owner, which is the outcome reading because a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot leave its count. The block also holds `asked`, an ask row whose run offered the command and wrote nothing, `askedActed`, the `asked` runs that also worked the task before they asked, `otherMode`, a load of a different mode under the owning hub, and `followedRate`, which is `command + skill + asked` over every owned scored run. `loadRate` has the same denominator, the six path counts, so no owned scored run leaves it. `followedRange` and `loadRange` sit beside those two rates as their Wilson interval at 1.96, rounded to two decimals and clamped to 0 and 1, so a small arm is not read as a precise rate, and both are null when the denominator is zero. `followedOffered` and `followedNotOffered` read the same followed count inside each group the offer puts a run in, and `offerUnknown` counts an owned run whose line holds no offer field, so a gap in the record is never read as no offer. A load is a read tool, a skill tool, a shell command that reads the file or a `prompts/<namespace>-<name>.md` mirror, and a write outside the run's checkout sets no boundary. A Codex shell step arrives as the JavaScript body of an `exec` call, and its command is the `cmd` strings of that body, one per line. A body that holds a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step. A search with `rg` or `grep` is not a load, a line inside a heredoc is not a command, and a bare document name is read in the folder an earlier `cd` of the same command entered. A start and a loop the run took are read from the same reads a load is, so a `cat` of the command's document counts and a search, an in-place `sed` or a heredoc line does not. A heredoc's end word may hold a hyphen or a dot. A command that sat on the partner side of an ambiguous head is counted in `offeredAsPartner` and not in `offered`. A stored run line holds no `offeredAs`, so its offer counts as before. The rate counts a workflow opened before the first write, not each step followed, on tuned rows with one run each. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:124:| `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. Each offer carries `offeredAs`, `head` or `partner`. A fallback head such as `Advisor: no skill matched.` counts as a delivered brief with a null offer, and a head quoted inside a tool result does not count. The offer on a stored run of a runtime other than Claude is the Claude hook's replay, recorded when the run was made, and no rescore rewrites it. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:188:The output log holds the same lines plus `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `offerError`, `briefDelivered` and `offerBackfilled`. Exit 2 means the output was refused, and the printed JSON names why: `same_path`, `holdout_row`, `unknown_row` or a missing `--out`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:53:  return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null, offerError };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:63: * `offeredAs` records whether the match sat before `vs` as the head or after\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:68: *   offeredAs: 'head' | 'partner' | null }}\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:74:    return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offeredAs: null };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:80:    offeredAs: text.slice(0, match.index).includes(' vs ') ? 'partner' : 'head',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:97: *   offeredAs: 'head' | 'partner' | null, offerError: string | null }}\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:414:export async function backfillRunLog({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:496:        offeredAs: offer.offeredAs ?? null,\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"offeredAs|backfillRunLog\\\" --glob '!**/command-prompts.jsonl' --glob '!**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680409507,"end":1794680410940}}}}
