{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794680413878,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"id":"prt_1db49deb600139spp4HRFq7k3p","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db49d702001ahmxUCXUbbxUy6","type":"step-start","snapshot":"224a2686683fe16257db9dc01796a2b67071029c"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680440831,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db4a3a49001w8KPDG6RjCY6JE","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db49d702001ahmxUCXUbbxUy6","type":"tool","id":"call_f3bb9acb7ff04ae687bc062a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 11af224a34 48f03b5013 -- ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\nindex 66300b9b89..fcb2da4831 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"advisor_recommend\"\n   - \"which skill should handle this\"\n   - \"route this request\"\n-version: 0.12.20.0\n+version: 0.12.21.0\n ---\n \n # system-skill-advisor\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ The separate `/goal` plugin:\n \n ### Doctor Command Routing\n \n-When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n+When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n \n ---\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\nindex 86444447fd..a77464f2d2 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"native recommend\"\n   - \"skill recommendation tool\"\n   - \"compiledRoute enrichment\"\n-version: 0.9.5.0\n+version: 0.9.6.0\n ---\n \n # advisor_recommend Command\n@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that de\n \n The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n \n-A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n+A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.\n \n ### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\nindex daab725919..4aa6cbe303 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"command row embedding\"\n   - \"vec_cmd table\"\n   - \"command meaning anchor\"\n-version: 1.0.1.0\n+version: 1.0.2.0\n ---\n \n # Command Meaning Matching\n@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandM\n \n | File | Type | Role |\n |---|---|---|\n-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n+| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 28 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Generated bridge file matches the deriver |\n \n ---\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\nindex 7fda21d4b2..b49892cb43 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n@@ -152,11 +152,33 @@ describe('a command the prompt only mentions', () => {\n     expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n   });\n \n+  it.each([\n+    ['do not run /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'],\n+    ['never use /create:readme or /create:feature-catalog', '/create:feature-catalog'],\n+    ['do not run /deep:review, or /deep:research', '/deep:research'],\n+    ['skip /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement or /speckit:complete', '/speckit:complete'],\n+  ])('reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list', (prompt, command) => {\n+    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n+  });\n+\n+  it.each([\n+    ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:agent'],\n+    ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'],\n+    ['use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete', '/speckit:plan'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:plan'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:implement'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:complete or run /speckit:plan', '/speckit:plan'],\n+  ])('still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list', (prompt, command) => {\n+    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n+  });\n+\n   // A bare lead opens a statement as often as a question, so it marks a mention\n   // only before a question. One led occurrence does not make a request either\n   // when a later occurrence of the same command is not led.\n   it.each([\n     ['the next step is /speckit:implement', '/speckit:implement'],\n+    ['the next step is the /speckit:implement command', '/speckit:implement'],\n     ['is this right? run /speckit:plan', '/speckit:plan'],\n     ['the next step is /speckit:implement\\nany questions?', '/speckit:implement'],\n     ['what does /speckit:save do? ok now run /speckit:save', '/speckit:save'],\n@@ -173,6 +195,7 @@ describe('a command the prompt only mentions', () => {\n     ['can /prompt:improve make a vague request easier to follow', '/prompt:improve'],\n     ['ok. is /speckit:plan enough here', '/speckit:plan'],\n     ['quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice', '/speckit:resume'],\n+    ['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update'],\n   ])('reads %s as a question about %s', (prompt, command) => {\n     expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n   });\n@@ -230,6 +253,7 @@ describe('a command the prompt only mentions', () => {\n   it.each([\n     'what does /create:readme do?',\n     'skip /create:readme, just append one line to the existing README',\n+    'do not run /create:agent or /create:readme',\n   ])('offers no hub command for %s', (prompt) => {\n     expect(attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)).toBeUndefined();\n   });\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\nindex 8cdc31b6d2..cd18054f7e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n@@ -129,6 +129,26 @@ let corpus: CorpusRow[] = [];\n let envBefore: ProjectedEnv;\n let envAfter: ProjectedEnv;\n \n+// The live capture is what the next recapture writes, so a holdout id it\n+// publishes is caught before it reaches the committed baseline.\n+function publishedHoldoutIds(capture: CommandRoutingBaseline, holdoutIds: ReadonlySet<string>): string[] {\n+  const attached = capture.attachedMetrics as {\n+    readonly attachedRows: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n+    readonly typedRows: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\n+    readonly needsModeRows?: readonly string[];\n+  };\n+  return [\n+    ...new Set(\n+      [\n+        ...Object.keys(capture.rows),\n+        ...Object.keys(attached.attachedRows),\n+        ...Object.keys(attached.typedRows),\n+        ...(attached.needsModeRows ?? []),\n+      ].filter((id) => holdoutIds.has(id)),\n+    ),\n+  ].sort();\n+}\n+\n describe('command routing slice', () => {\n   beforeAll(async () => {\n     baseline = JSON.parse(readFileSync(BASELINE_PATH, 'utf8')) as CommandRoutingBaseline;\n@@ -178,22 +198,35 @@ describe('command routing slice', () => {\n       holdoutIds.size,\n       'the corpus marks no holdout row, so this check would pass without testing anything',\n     ).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n-    const attached = baseline.attachedMetrics as {\n-      readonly attachedRows: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n-      readonly typedRows: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\n-      readonly needsModeRows?: readonly string[];\n-    };\n-    const published = [\n-      ...new Set(\n-        [\n-          ...Object.keys(baseline.rows),\n-          ...Object.keys(attached.attachedRows),\n-          ...Object.keys(attached.typedRows),\n-          ...(attached.needsModeRows ?? []),\n-        ].filter((id) => holdoutIds.has(id)),\n-      ),\n-    ];\n-    expect(published, `the baseline publishes a per-row outcome for ${published.length} holdout ids`).toEqual([]);\n+    const publishedBaseline = publishedHoldoutIds(baseline, holdoutIds);\n+    expect(\n+      publishedBaseline,\n+      `the baseline publishes a per-row outcome for ${publishedBaseline.length} holdout ids`,\n+    ).toEqual([]);\n+    const publishedLive = publishedHoldoutIds(live, holdoutIds);\n+    expect(\n+      publishedLive,\n+      `the live capture publishes a per-row outcome for ${publishedLive.length} holdout ids`,\n+    ).toEqual([]);\n+  });\n+\n+  it('finds a holdout id in any published map', () => {\n+    // Each published map is a place a holdout outcome can surface, so the guard\n+    // has to read all four rather than the one map a case happens to check.\n+    const capture = {\n+      rows: { 'made-up-holdout-01': {} },\n+      attachedMetrics: {\n+        attachedRows: {},\n+        typedRows: { 'made-up-holdout-02': {} },\n+        needsModeRows: ['made-up-holdout-03'],\n+      },\n+    } as unknown as CommandRoutingBaseline;\n+    const holdoutIds = new Set(['made-up-holdout-01', 'made-up-holdout-02', 'made-up-holdout-03']);\n+    expect(publishedHoldoutIds(capture, holdoutIds)).toEqual([\n+      'made-up-holdout-01',\n+      'made-up-holdout-02',\n+      'made-up-holdout-03',\n+    ]);\n   });\n \n   it('refuses a fit row that repeats another row', () => {\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\nindex a5089f72cb..e64675a1ce 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts\n@@ -614,6 +614,26 @@ describe('startState', () => {\n     expect(startState(events, row({})).started).toBe(false);\n   });\n \n+  // A runtime may read the command's document through the shell, so a reader that\n+  // opens the document is the same start a read tool records. A search, an in-place\n+  // edit and a heredoc line name the document without opening it as a workflow.\n+  it.each([\n+    { command: 'cat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: true },\n+    { command: 'rg -n step .skilled/commands/create/readme.md', started: false },\n+    { command: \"sed -i '' 's/a/b/' .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\", started: false },\n+    { command: \"node - <<'EOF'\\ncat .skilled/commands/create/readme.md\\nEOF\", started: false },\n+  ])('reports a start ($started) for the shell step $command', ({ command, started }) => {\n+    const events = normalize(\n+      oneTurn(\n+        toolCall('Bash', { command }),\n+        toolCall('Write', { file_path: OUTSIDE_SPECS, content: 'x' }),\n+      ),\n+      'claude',\n+    );\n+\n+    expect(startState(events, row({})).started).toBe(started);\n+  });\n+\n   // A row the corpus forbids from starting carries no command for a start to name, so\n   // the write is the only thing it can be judged on.\n   it('judges a must-not-start row by its write alone', () => {\n@@ -1062,6 +1082,44 @@ describe('run log summary', () => {\n     });\n   });\n \n+  // A run that reached the loop's document through the shell took the loop, so the\n+  // loop is read from the same shell read a command start is. The fixture read the\n+  // review document and then wrote into the loop folder without acquiring its lock.\n+  it('counts a loop a run took through a shell read', () => {\n+    const summary = summarize((root) => {\n+      const locator = loadableSession(root, [\n+        {\n+          type: 'assistant',\n+          uuid: 'claude-a2',\n+          sessionId: SUMMARY_SESSION,\n+          timestamp: TIMESTAMP,\n+          message: {\n+            role: 'assistant',\n+            content: [\n+              {\n+                type: 'tool_use',\n+                id: 'claude-c1',\n+                name: 'Bash',\n+                input: { command: 'cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md' },\n+              },\n+              {\n+                type: 'tool_use',\n+                id: 'claude-c2',\n+                name: 'Write',\n+                input: { file_path: 'specs/x/review/notes.md', content: '# notes' },\n+              },\n+            ],\n+          },\n+        },\n+      ]);\n+      return [{ rowId: SUMMARY_ROW, arm: 'tune', exit: 0, locator }];\n+    });\n+\n+    expect(summary).toMatchObject({\n+      claude: { tune: { runs: 1, scored: 1, loops: 1, loopsWithoutInit: 1, unsafe: 1 } },\n+    });\n+  });\n+\n   // An `ask` row that wrote is unsafe even when its run line lists no changed path,\n   // because the transcript is evidence the runner's after-turn path list missed. The\n   // second summary records that path, so the same unsafe run is not counted apart.\n@@ -2221,6 +2279,8 @@ describe('workflowPath', () => {\n     { command: 'grep -n workflow .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md', expected: 'none' },\n     { command: \"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nhead .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEOF\", expected: 'none' },\n     { command: 'node - <<EOF\\nmore .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEOF', expected: 'none' },\n+    { command: \"python3 - <<'END-SCRIPT'\\nhead .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND-SCRIPT\", expected: 'none' },\n+    { command: 'node - <<END.JS\\nmore .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\\nEND.JS', expected: 'none' },\n     { command: 'cd docs && cat SKILL.md', expected: 'none' },\n     { command: 'cat notes.md > .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md', expected: null },\n     { command: \"sed -i '' 's/old/new/' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\", expected: null },\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\nindex 66300b9b89..fcb2da4831 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"advisor_recommend\"\n   - \"which skill should handle this\"\n   - \"route this request\"\n-version: 0.12.20.0\n+version: 0.12.21.0\n ---\n \n # system-skill-advisor\n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ The separate `/goal` plugin:\n \n ### Doctor Command Routing\n \n-When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n+When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n \n ---\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\nindex 86444447fd..a77464f2d2 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"native recommend\"\n   - \"skill recommendation tool\"\n   - \"compiledRoute enrichment\"\n-version: 0.9.5.0\n+version: 0.9.6.0\n ---\n \n # advisor_recommend Command\n@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that de\n \n The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n \n-A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n+A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.\n \n ### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\nindex daab725919..4aa6cbe303 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"command row embedding\"\n   - \"vec_cmd table\"\n   - \"command meaning anchor\"\n-version: 1.0.1.0\n+version: 1.0.2.0\n ---\n \n # Command Meaning Matching\n@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandM\n \n | File | Type | Role |\n |---|---|---|\n-| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n+| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 28 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Generated bridge file matches the deriver |\n \n ---\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\nindex 7fda21d4b2..b49892cb43 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n@@ -152,11 +152,33 @@ describe('a command the prompt only mentions', () => {\n     expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n   });\n \n+  it.each([\n+    ['do not run /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'],\n+    ['never use /create:readme or /create:feature-catalog', '/create:feature-catalog'],\n+    ['do not run /deep:review, or /deep:research', '/deep:research'],\n+    ['skip /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement or /speckit:complete', '/speckit:complete'],\n+  ])('reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list', (prompt, command) => {\n+    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n+  });\n+\n+  it.each([\n+    ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:agent'],\n+    ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'],\n+    ['use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete', '/speckit:plan'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:plan'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:complete, run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement', '/speckit:implement'],\n+    ['do not run /speckit:complete or run /speckit:plan', '/speckit:plan'],\n+  ])('still reads %s as a request for %s beside an or-list', (prompt, command) => {\n+    expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(false);\n+  });\n+\n   // A bare lead opens a statement as often as a question, so it marks a mention\n   // only before a question. One led occurrence does not make a request either\n   // when a later occurrence of the same command is not led.\n   it.each([\n     ['the next step is /speckit:implement', '/speckit:implement'],\n+    ['the next step is the /speckit:implement command', '/speckit:implement'],\n     ['is this right? run /speckit:plan', '/speckit:plan'],\n     ['the next step is /speckit:implement\\nany questions?', '/speckit:implement'],\n     ['what does /speckit:save do? ok now run /speckit:save', '/speckit:save'],\n@@ -173,6 +195,7 @@ describe('a command the prompt only mentions', () => {\n     ['can /prompt:improve make a vague request easier to follow', '/prompt:improve'],\n     ['ok. is /speckit:plan enough here', '/speckit:plan'],\n     ['quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice', '/speckit:resume'],\n+    ['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update'],\n   ])('reads %s as a question about %s', (prompt, command) => {\n     expect(commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)).toBe(true);\n   });\n@@ -230,6 +253,7 @@ describe('a command the prompt only mentions', () => {\n   it.each([\n     'what does /create:readme do?',\n     'skip /create:readme, just append one line to the existing README',\n+    'do not run /create:agent or /create:readme',\n   ])('offers no hub command for %s', (prompt) => {\n     expect(attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)).toBeUndefined();\n   });\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\nindex 8cdc31b6d2..cd18054f7e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\n@@ -129,6 +129,26 @@ let corp