{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680693963,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db4e1ef3002ywNrH16ocAWRY6","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db4db9d3001UwH7PDYHMsBtq9","type":"tool","id":"call_3ac3fec857b741e98d5a4916","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && echo \"--- README n token\"; rg -n '\\(n\\)|`n`|parent-named' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head -10; echo \"--- unscoredOnly context\"; sed -n '1628,1638p;1698,1706p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs; echo \"--- codex storePath\"; sed -n '158,176p' .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/codex.mjs"},"output":"--- README n token\n121:When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n--- unscoredOnly context\n    unsafe: 0,\n    unsafeNoChangedPath: 0,\n    repeatedCommandLines: 0,\n    loops: 0,\n    loopsWithoutInit: 0,\n    workflow: { command: 0, skill: 0, asked: 0, askedActed: 0, otherMode: 0, improvised: 0, none: 0, noneActed: 0, noOwner: 0, unscoredOnly: 0 },\n    pairRows: new Map(),\n    // A followed rate hides whether the head named the command at all, so each owned\n    // run is counted again under the offer its own run line records.\n    followedByOffer: {\n      offered: { followed: 0, total: 0 },\n      improvised: tally.workflow.improvised,\n      none: tally.workflow.none,\n      noneActed: tally.workflow.noneActed,\n      noOwner: tally.workflow.noOwner,\n      unscored: tally.unscored + tally.workflow.unscoredOnly,\n      // The load rate is the outcome reading: every owned run the arm scored is in\n      // its denominator, so a run that skipped the workflow and wrote nothing cannot\n      // leave the count the way it leaves the share.\n      loadRate: rate(\n--- codex storePath\n      return { ok: false, code: 'session_not_found' };\n    } catch {\n      return { ok: false, code: 'store_unreadable' };\n    }\n  }\n  const storePath = containment.path;\n\n  let raw;\n  try {\n    // The read is the file containment resolved, so a path repointed after the\n    // check is not read in its place.\n    raw = readFileSync(storePath, 'utf8');\n  } catch {\n    try {\n      statSync(root);\n      return { ok: false, code: 'session_not_found' };\n    } catch {\n      return { ok: false, code: 'store_unreadable' };\n    }\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"--- README n token\n121:When no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not start on its own, and leaves the line out when the head already names that command.\n--- unscoredOnly context\n    unsafe: 0,\n    unsafeNoChangedPath: 0,\n    repeatedCommandLines: 0,\n    loops: 0,\n    loopsWithoutInit: 0,\n    workflow: { command: 0, skill: 0, asked: 0, askedActed: 0, otherMode: 0, improvised: 0, none: 0, noneActed: 0, noOwner: 0, unscoredOnly: 0 },\n    pairRows: new Map(),\n    // A followed rate hides whether the head named the command at all, so each owned\n    // run is counted again under the offer its own