+0 P1, +0 P2\n+- **P1 (Major):** 1 active\n+- **P2 (Minor):** 3 active\n+- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +1 P1, +3 P2\n+- **Open IDs:** SAC4B-P1-001, SAC4B-P2-001, SAC4B-P2-002, iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field (carried, fix not applied)\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n \n ---\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":3}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\",\"newString\":\"- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 1 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 3 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +1 P1, +3 P2\\n- **Open IDs:** SAC4B-P1-001, SAC4B-P2-001, SAC4B-P2-002, iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field (carried, fix not applied)\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680838627,"end":1794680843299}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680843304,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db50614c001H0P8Sbm6OXLtFv","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db50414b001sHPuCX1mIkkTFr","type":"tool","id":"call_ff053582cf7d479b8f36aac0","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Importing `command-attach.ts` directly with Node's type stripping: it is the actual module, so a gate result is observed behavior rather than a regex reading (iteration 1).\n- Pairing each brief check with its pinning test row: it separates \"the fix holds\" from \"the test only covers the easy form\" (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the or-list tests as proof of the whole class: all five rows use a bare `/cmd or /cmd` shape, so the article form stayed invisible until the probe (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -95,15 +95,16 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Importing `command-attach.ts` directly with Node's type stripping: it is the actual module, so a gate result is observed behavior rather than a regex reading (iteration 1).\n+- Pairing each brief check with its pinning test row: it separates \"the fix holds\" from \"the test only covers the easy form\" (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the or-list tests as proof of the whole class: all five rows use a bare `/cmd or /cmd` shape, so the article form stayed invisible until the probe (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration — populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Importing `command-attach.ts` directly with Node's type stripping: it is the actual module, so a gate result is observed behavior rather than a regex reading (iteration 1).\\n- Pairing each brief check with its pinning test row: it separates \\\"the fix holds\\\" from \\\"the test only covers the easy form\\\" (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Reading the or-lis