{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794680982718,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db528037001sbMTdQAM6P0HVY","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db520b7e001k4dc0Aoz79bxVs","type":"tool","id":"call_ac25bf87132f4db3af714ec5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '118,126p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | cut -c1-400; echo \"--- paired paragraph\"; rg -n \"paired\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head -10"},"output":"\n### Doctor Command Routing\n\nWhen no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not \n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n--- paired paragraph\n32:When a runtime meets an ambiguous prompt, guessing which skill to dispatch silently misroutes work. Guessing also hides the reason, so a bad route cannot be explained or repaired. And hook code that echoes the user prompt into logs creates a privacy problem that scales with every invocation.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n### Doctor Command Routing\n\nWhen no skill answers a setup or health prompt, the fallback names the runnable `/doctor:setup` line. When a skill and doctor bridge both pass without a typed `/doctor:` command, the skill stays first and the brief adds `Also: /doctor:<command> <target> (<policy>)` as its second line, where the policy is run, start or ask, or `parent-named only` in a child session for a command the child must not \n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n--- paired paragraph\n32:When a runtime meets an ambiguous prompt, guessing which skill to dispatch silently misroutes work. Guessing also hides the reason, so a bad route cannot be explained or repaired. And hook code that echoes the user prompt into logs creates a privacy problem that scales with every invocation.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '118,126p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | cut -c1-400; echo \\\"--- paired paragraph\\\"; rg -n \\\"paired\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794680979511,"end":1794680982718}}}}
