{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681017018,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db530c1a001DHjQI3SL5uVhLZ","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db52e1290010v8hb5bqzvSH2c","type":"tool","id":"call_67d64d78e69e496687caa3ef","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls specs/system-skill-advisor/; echo \"--- grep spec.md for P041\"; rg -n \"P041\" specs --glob 'spec.md' | head -10; echo \"--- grep tasks for T017 in advisor\"; rg -n \"T017\" specs/system-skill-advisor --glob 'tasks.md' | head -10"},"output":"codebase-conformance\ndescription.json\ngraph-metadata.json\nhost-integrations\nrouting-and-scoring\nruntime-lifecycle\nz_archive\n--- grep spec.md for P041\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:145:| 26 | 026-untuned-behaviour-arm/ | The behaviour arm on requests nobody tuned for: 36 fresh rows written blind and frozen by hash, each run twice with the advisor off and on at one commit on all six runtimes, 864 sessions, judged by a target fixed before the first session: a pooled exact sign test below 0.05, no command started on a decline row and the sealed reach floor, with a read-only step reader on 24 sessions and the B-5 decision taken from the printed counts. It runs after phase 027 and before phase 025 (operator decisions Q061 and Q063, Fable decisions P033 to P041, P044) | Pending |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:41:This is **Phase 26** of the build that makes the skill advisor surface every tracked slash command with a run, start or ask policy on every supported CLI (`../spec.md`). The operator's need is that models stay free to choose and still take the right workflow more often. Phase 023 showed that no stored arm can say whether the brief causes that: the rows were tuned, each ran once, and the two arms differed in more than the brief (`../023-untuned-outcome-evidence/scratch/outcome-evidence.txt:31-35`). The operator approved a new arm on all six runtimes, Codex included (Q061), at 864 sessions (Q063). A Fable 5.2 session decided its design and its target (`../review/fable-decisions-2026-11-14/report.txt` sections 1, 2, 5 and 6, decisions P033 to P041). This phase plans that design and does not change it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:151:- Give the live brief cost a number or a decline, as the first task (P041).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:160:- Raising the sealed reach, the fit decline count of 8 of 24 and the advisory on eight sealed rows - the follow-up packet owns them (Q060, P041).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:200:| REQ-005 | The live brief cost is a number from `measure-brief-cost.mjs` or a decline that quotes its refusal, recorded before any other task runs (P041). |\n--- grep tasks for T017 in advisor\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/009-test-findings-remediation/tasks.md:69:- [x] T017 Rebuild the advisor dist and run the advisor suite and typecheck, the plugin tests, the Pi dispatch suite, the stress pair and the 457 harness, serially. Evidence, from the final state after F21: typecheck exit 0; advisor suite 127 files, 959 passed, 6 skipped, 0 failed; plugin tests 31 of 31; Pi dispatch 50 of 50; spec-kit hook files 236 passed, 7 skipped, 0 failed; stress 6 of 6; the 457 harness `passed: true` for claude, codex, cursor and devin. The live generation and launcher state files were byte-identical before and after each run.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/012-reverify-follow-ups/tasks.md:66:- [x] T017 Round 1: rerun CP-003 on the first teardown in the five CLIs, one at a time (`evidence/teardown-reruns/round-1/`)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/007-docs-and-standards-alignment/tasks.md:64:- [x] T017 Run `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the packet and require `RESULT: PASSED`. Evidence: exit 0, all eight folders `RESULT: PASSED` with 0 errors and 0 warnings, after `repair-derived.cjs --apply` refreshed the stale graph fingerprints.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/003-hook-path-cli-spawn-trim/tasks.md:65:- [x] T017 Over a debug-on window, compare median hook `durationMs` on compiled-hub turns against T003. Evidence: paired hook A/B on one build and one daemon, 45 pairs, enrichment off saves a median 65 ms per turn and is faster in 35 pairs; CLI A/B on an isolated daemon, 1,097 to 1,021 ms. See the implementation summary for why the comparison is paired rather than against the four-sample T003 window.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/010-review-advisories-and-codex-cleanup/tasks.md:58:- [x] T017 R3-P2-002, R1-P2-003: move the close-out into `synthesis-closeout.cjs` and fold review lineage logs (`system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/`, `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/`). Verified: 11 fixture pairs give the old program's event and exit code, 115 tests pass and the lineage test fails against base\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/014-changelog-alignment/tasks.md:65:- [x] T017 Recheck `git status` and stage only this phase's paths with `--pathspec-from-file`, leaving every other session's file unstaged. The commit, the trigger index rebuild and the push follow, and goal criterion 6 covers them\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/011-observation-fixes/tasks.md:65:- [x] T017 Strict validation of the 13 other folders matches the T002 baseline: 10 PASSED and 3 scratch FAILED before and after, with one warning fewer in each quarantine folder (`evidence/validate-other-folders.txt`)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/codebase-conformance/003-align-runtime-code-with-sk-code-skilled/tasks.md:61:- [x] T017 Move `lib/test-helpers/` to `tests/helpers/`, because test helpers belong under `tests/` and the production build was shipping this one in `dist` [EVIDENCE: `env-snapshot.ts` and its README moved; the one importer, `stress-test/skill-advisor/opencode-plugin-bridge-stress.vitest.ts`, repointed; README retitled; `tests/README.md` tree lists `helpers/`; the stale `dist/runtime/lib/test-helpers` build output removed; advisor typecheck exit 0; the stress file loads and passes 3 of 4, and its one failure is sa-034, which also fails on main]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/codebase-conformance/003-align-runtime-code-with-sk-code-skilled/tasks.md:129:- [x] CHK-023 [P1] Each merge followed by `rg` for the old path returning nothing [EVIDENCE: T007-T013 and T017: `rg` for each old path (`lib/context/`, `lib/corpus/`, `lib/routing/`, `tests/utils/`, `lanes/__tests__/`, `__fixtures__`, `__shared__`, `lib/test-helpers/`) returns nothing in code]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/012-advisor-doc-trigger-harvest/tasks.md:82:- [x] T017 Isolated pilot against the real skill tree (temp `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`): scan 355/84 docs; deep-loop-runtime's 4 references row-verified; \"deep loop script interface contract\" → deep-loop-runtime top candidate (0.2968) with `doc:references/script_interface_contract.md`; flag-off probe: 0 skills with docTriggers (`/tmp/pilot-doc-harvest2.mjs`, `/tmp/pilot3.mjs`)\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"codebase-conformance\ndescription.json\ngraph-metadata.json\nhost-integrations\nrouting-and-scoring\nruntime-lifecycle\nz_archive\n--- grep spec.md for P041\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:145:| 26 | 026-untuned-behaviour-arm/ | The behaviour arm on requests nobody tuned for: 36 fresh rows written blind and frozen by hash, each run twice with the advisor off and on at one commit on all six runtimes, 864 sessions, judged by a target fixed before the first session: a pooled exact sign test below 0.05, no command started on a decline row and the sealed reach floor, with a read-only step reader on 24 sessions and the B-5 decision taken from the printed counts. It runs after phase 027 and before phase 025 (operator decisions Q061 and Q063, Fable decisions P033 to P041, P044) | Pending |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:41:This is **Phase 26** of the build that makes the skill advisor surface every tracked slash command with a run, start or ask policy on every supported CLI (`../spec.md`). The operator's need is that models stay free to choose and still take the right workflow more often. Phase 023 showed that no stored arm can say whether the brief causes that: the rows were tuned, each ran once, and the two arms differed in more than the brief (`../023-untuned-outcome-evidence/scratch/outcome-evidence.txt:31-35`). The operator approved a new arm on all six runtimes, Codex included (Q061), at 864 sessions (Q063). A Fable 5.2 session decided its design and its target (`../review/fable-decisions-2026-11-14/report.txt` sections 1, 2, 5 and 6, decisions P033 to P041). This phase plans that design and does not change it.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:151:- Give the live brief cost a number or a decline, as the first task (P041).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:160:- Raising the sealed reach, the fit decline count of 8 of 24 and the advisory on eight sealed rows - the follow-up packet owns them (Q060, P041).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/026-untuned-behaviour-arm/spec.md:200:| REQ-005 | The live brief cost is a number from `measure-brief-cost.mjs` or a decline that quotes its refusal, recorded before any other task runs (P041). |\n--- grep tasks for T017 in advisor\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/009-test-findings-remediation/tasks.md:69:- [x] T017 Rebuild the advisor dist and run the advisor suite and typecheck, the plugin tests, the Pi dispatch suite, the stress pair and the 457 harness, serially. Evidence, from the final state after F21: typecheck exit 0; advisor suite 127 files, 959 passed, 6 skipped, 0 failed; plugin tests 31 of 31; Pi dispatch 50 of 50; spec-kit hook files 236 passed, 7 skipped, 0 failed; stress 6 of 6; the 457 harness `passed: true` for claude, codex, cursor and devin. The live generation and launcher state files were byte-identical before and after each run.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/012-reverify-follow-ups/tasks.md:66:- [x] T017 Round 1: rerun CP-003 on the first teardown in the five CLIs, one at a time (`evidence/teardown-reruns/round-1/`)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/007-docs-and-standards-alignment/tasks.md:64:- [x] T017 Run `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the packet and require `RESULT: PASSED`. Evidence: exit 0, all eight folders `RESULT: PASSED` with 0 errors and 0 warnings, after `repair-derived.cjs --apply` refreshed the stale graph fingerprints.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/003-hook-path-cli-spawn-trim/tasks.md:65:- [x] T017 Over a debug-on window, compare median hook `durationMs` on compiled-hub turns against T003. Evidence: paired hook A/B on one build and one daemon, 45 pairs, enrichment off saves a median 65 ms per turn and is faster in 35 pairs; CLI A/B on an isolated daemon, 1,097 to 1,021 ms. See the implementation summary for why the comparison is paired rather than against the four-sample T003 window.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/010-review-advisories-and-codex-cleanup/tasks.md:58:- [x] T017 R3-P2-002, R1-P2-003: move the close-out into `synthesis-closeout.cjs` and fold review lineage logs (`system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/`, `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/`). Verified: 11 fixture pairs give the old program's event and exit code, 115 tests pass and the lineage test fails against base\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/014-changelog-alignment/tasks.md:65:- [x] T017 Recheck `git status` and stage only this phase's paths with `--pathspec-from-file`, leaving every other session's file unstaged. The commit, the trigger index rebuild and the push follow, and goal criterion 6 covers them\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/011-observation-fixes/tasks.md:65:- [x] T017 Strict validation of the 13 other folders matches the T002 baseline: 10 PASSED and 3 scratch FAILED before and after, with one warning fewer in each quarantine folder (`evidence/validate-other-folders.txt`)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/codebase-conformance/003-align-runtime-code-with-sk-code-skilled/tasks.md:61:- [x] T017 Move `lib/test-helpers/` to `tests/helpers/`, because test helpers belong under `tests/` and the production build was shipping this one in `dist` [EVIDENCE: `env-snapshot.ts` and its README moved; the one importer, `stress-test/skill-advisor/opencode-plugin-bridge-stress.vitest.ts`, repointed; README retitled; `tests/README.md` tree lists `helpers/`; the stale `dist/runtime/lib/test-helpers` build output removed; advisor typecheck exit 0; the stress file loads and passes 3 of 4, and its one failure is sa-034, which also fails on main]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/codebase-conformance/003-align-runtime-code-with-sk-code-skilled/tasks.md:129:- [x] CHK-023 [P1] Each merge followed by `rg` for the old path returning nothing [EVIDENCE: T007-T013 and T017: `rg` for each old path (`lib/context/`, `lib/corpus/`, `lib/routing/`, `tests/utils/`, `lanes/__tests__/`, `__fixtures__`, `__shared__`, `lib/test-helpers/`) returns nothing in code]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/012-advisor-doc-trigger-harvest/tasks.md:82:- [x] T017 Isolated pilot against the real skill tree (temp `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`): scan 355/84 docs; deep-loop-runtime's 4 references row-verified; \"deep loop script interface contract\" → deep-loop-runtime top candidate (0.2968) with `doc:references/script_interface_contract.md`; flag-off probe: 0 skills with docTriggers (`/tmp/pilot-doc-harvest2.mjs`, `/tmp/pilot3.mjs`)\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls specs/system-skill-advisor/; echo \\\"--- grep spec.md for P041\\\"; rg -n \\\"P041\\\" specs --glob 'spec.md' | head -10; echo \\\"--- grep tasks for T017 in advisor\\\"; rg -n \\\"T017\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor --glob 'tasks.md' | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681015322,"end":1794681017018}}}}
