ompt that names no command returns `false` from `commandOnlyMentioned` and changes no row.\n- Maximum input: a prompt that names two commands is read once per command, so `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` keeps the first and withholds the second.\n- Failure path: a prompt that asks about a command and then asks for it with a pronoun (`what does /create:readme do? run it on the hooks folder`) loses the command and keeps `sk-doc`. A retired name such as `/create:skill` is not read as a mention of its successor and keeps today's behaviour.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Scope 6/25: one option in `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"001-command-routing-baseline-corpus/\n002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/\n003-plain-chat-command-reach/\n004-command-meaning-matching/\n005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/\n006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/\n007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/\n009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/\n010-reachability-and-attribution/\n011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/\n012-plain-offer-reach/\n013-attribution-and-install-reach/\n014-review-remediation/\n015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/\n016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/\n017-review-pass-two-remediation/\n018-holdout-row-retirement/\n019-workflow-outcome-measure/\n020-command-offer-fit-guards/\n021-brief-head-parity/\n022-workflow-measure-soundness/\n023-untuned-outcome-evidence/\n024-fable-review-remediation/\n025-release-notes-and-doc-sync/\n026-untuned-behaviour-arm/\n027-review-pass-four-remediation/\nreview/\nscratch/\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n## L2: EDGE CASES\n<!-- FILL: Name the empty input, the maximum input and the failure path. One line each. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Empty input: an empty `logs/archive/` deletes nothing and exits 0. Maximum: `--keep 3` over 10,000 archives keeps the newest 3. Failure path: a missing `--keep` value exits 2 with usage. WEAK: Handle edge cases. -->\n\n- Empty input: an empty prompt or a prompt that names no command returns `false` from `commandOnlyMentioned` and changes no row.\n- Maximum input: a prompt that names two commands is read once per command, so `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` keeps the first and withholds the second.\n- Failure path: a prompt that asks about a command and then asks for it with a pronoun (`what does /create:readme do? run it on the hooks folder`) loses the command and keeps `sk-doc`. A retired name such as `/create:skill` is not read as a mention of its successor and keeps today's behaviour.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Scope 6/25: one option in `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && ls -d */ | head -40; echo \\\"---\\\"; sed -n '236,250p' 020*/spec.md 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-500\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681022541,"end":1794681023406}}}}
