 small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-doc', 'sk-create-agent', 'build an agent that fixes typos in our docs'], ['sk-doc', 'sk-create-readme', 'writing a readme for the grammar module'], ['sk-doc', 'sk-create-readme', 'add a readme for the spelling package'], ['sk-doc',\n80:- [x] T022 Withhold a creation command only on a correction verb, and exempt the changelog and goal commands (`CA`, `CAG`). After T021, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T021 found that changelog, goal and noun-led requests still lose their command, decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-create-changelog', 'changelog for v2.1, it fixes the broken link checker and spelling errors'], ['sk-create-changelog', 'log the spelling fixes in the changelog'], ['sk-create-readme', 'document the cli in a r\n81:- [x] T024 Gate only the document commands a small edit corrects in place (`CA`, `CAG`). After T022, before T020. Added after the third Opus check of the small-edit gate found that a request for an agent, skill or command whose purpose names a correction (`an agent to fix typos`) lost its command. Three fixes of one symptom reached the retry bound, so the design is inverted once, decided without the operator (D1): if this check also finds a common miss, the gate is removed instead. Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-create-agent', '\n82:- [x] T026 Leave the repo-rule and benchmark commands out of the small-edit gate (`CA`, `CAG`). After T024, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T024 (PASS) found that a repo rule or a benchmark names its purpose the way an agent does, so `I want a repo rule that says fix typos in the same commit` lost `/create:repo-rule`. Decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each(['I want a repo rule that says fix typos in the same commit', 'repo rule: always fix typos in the same commit'])('keeps the repo-rule command o\n88:- [x] T008 Add the gate that stops a mentioned command's own row (`FU`, `CMA`). Start after T003 is verified. This task adds the function `withholdMentionedCommands` and nothing else. T017 and T018 change the two functions that use the reader. Test first: in `CMA`, add `describe('withholdMentionedCommands')` with a passing command row `command-speckit-complete` and a passing skill row `system-spec-kit`, built with the row helper the neighbouring cases use. Expect `withholdMentionedCommands(rows, 'do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does')` to return the command row with `\n89:- [x] T017 Leave a refused typed command's owner where it ranked (`FU`, `TCO`). After T008. This task changes the function `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst` and nothing else. Test first: in `TCO`, inside `describe('a typed command without a scorer row leads through its owner')`, add `it('keeps the order when the prompt refuses the typed command')` with `const ranked = [recommendation('sk-code'), recommendation('sk-doc'), recommendation('sk-prompt')];` expecting `rankedSkills(ranked, 'do not run /create:goal')` to equal `['sk-code', 'sk-doc', 'sk-prompt']`. Run `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owne\n90:- [x] T018 Call the mention gate from the scoring function (`FU`). After T017. This task adds one line to the function `scoreAdvisorPrompt` and nothing else. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, find the statement that starts `ranked = applyDoctorHelperHandoff(ranked, {` and ends with `});`, and add on the line directly after that `});` the statement `ranked = withholdMentionedCommands(ranked, prompt);`. The next line stays `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);`. Verify: `rg -c -F 'ranked = withholdMentionedCommands(ranked, prompt);' $FU` prints 1, `rg -A1 -F 'ranked = withholdMent\n187:- [x] CHK-022 [P0] Each of T003 to T010 and T017 recorded a failing first run for the reason its line names. Evidenc