e needs (T010, T011) |\n     6\t\n     7\t---\n     8\t|----|-------------|\n     9\t| REQ-004 | `update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return `sk-doc` with no command, and `write a readme for the doctor scripts folder` still returns `sk-doc` with `/create:readme`. The gate covers correction wording only: an edit that names no correction word keeps its command and is listed under Out of Scope. |\n    10\t| REQ-005 | A meaning-passed command row whose uncertainty is above the threshold does not pass, so `document the new skill and create a feature catalog for it` leads with `sk-doc`. |\n    11\t| REQ-006 | On a no-edit request no command row of class `add-only` or `mutates` passes, and a `read-only` command row still passes. |\n    12\t| REQ-007 | A weak problem cue with no passing skill hands off only at ranker score 10 or more, so the two app-problem prompts return no recommendation and the three weak-cue toolkit prompts in the probe keep their doctor command. |\n    13\t| REQ-008 | No code comment added by this phase names a spec path, a phase, a task, a finding or a requirement id. |\n    14\t\n    15\t> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n    16\t> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n--- AC-007\n62:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given a weak problem cue and no passing skill, When the ranker scores below 10, Then no doctor command is handed off, and at 10 or more it is | Observed: `npx vitest run tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  16 passed (16)` and both app-problem prompts print `(no recommendation)` in `scratch/repro-after.txt`. The weak cue has its own bar of 9 (`tasks.md:93`, `tasks.md:95`) | Met | - |\n63-| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given the phase diff, When added comment lines are searched for a spec path or an id, Then nothing is found and only seven files changed | Observed: the comment id search in `scratch/boundaries.txt` exited 1 and the AGENTS.md and package checks printed nothing. Eight files changed, the seven named plus `command-routing-baseline.json`, recaptured under decision P020 in `../decision-record.md` (`tasks.md:110`) | Met | - |\n64-| AC-009 | REQ-001 | Given the whole advisor suite, When it runs after the build, Then it reports 0 failed with more passed tests than before | Observed: `scratch/after.txt` holds 1919 passed, 6 skipped and 0 failed over 184 of 184 files, against 1838 passed before (`tasks.md:107`) | Met | - |\n65-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"     1\t| A-8, B-9 first half, B-3 question case | `typedCommandForTop` and `attachCommand` attach any command the prompt names, and the command's own scorer row passes on the typed string | `commandOnlyMentioned` reads a refusal or a question about the command, and all three paths withhold it (T003 to T005, T008, T017, T018) |\n     2\t| B-3 edit case | A hub route that picks the README mode attaches `/create:readme` whatever the size of the edit | `attachCommand` withholds a `/create:*` command when the prompt names a correction, such as a typo, a spelling or a broken link (T006). An edit that names no correction word is not gated |\n     3\t| A-4 | `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` lifts a meaning match to the confidence bar and keeps its uncertainty of 0.42, above the 0.35 the hooks use | The meaning pass holds the uncertainty bar, so the scorer and the hooks agree (T007) |\n     4\t| A-6 | `/doctor:speckit` and `/doctor:deep-loop` are `run` commands of class `add-only`, and neither the phrase path nor the hand-off checks the no-edit request | Every command row that is not `read-only` stops passing on a no-edit request (T009) |\n     5\t| A-5, the two prompts with only a doctor row | A weak cue with no passing skill needs only the ranker score 6 | A weak cue needs the score 10 that a prompt with no cue needs (T010, T011) |\n     6\t\n     7\t---\n     8\t|----|-------------|\n     9\t| REQ-004 | `update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return `sk-doc` with no command, and `write a readme for the doctor scripts folder` still returns `sk-doc` with `/create:readme`. The gate covers correction wording only: an edit that names no correction word keeps its command and is listed under Out of Scope. |\n    10\t| REQ-005 | A meaning-passed command row whose uncertainty is above the threshold does not pass, so `document the new skill and create a feature catalog for it` leads with `sk-doc`. |\n    11\t| REQ-006 | On a no-edit request no command row of class `add-only` or `mutates` passes, and a `read-only` command row still passes. |\n    12\t| REQ-007 | A weak problem cue with no passing skill hands off only at ranker score 10 or more, so the two app-problem prompts return no recommendation and the three weak-cue toolkit prompts in the probe keep their doctor command. |\n    13\t| REQ-008 | No code comment added by this phase names a spec path, a phase, a task, a finding or a requirement id. |\n    14\t\n    15\t> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n    16\t> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n--- AC-007\n62:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given a weak problem cue and no passing skill, When the ranker scores below 10, Then no doctor command is handed off, and at 10 or more it is | Observed: `npx vitest run tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  16 passed (16)` and both app-problem prompts print `(no recommendation)` in `scratch/repro-after.txt`. The weak cue has its own bar of 9 (`tasks.md:93`, `tasks.md:95`) | Met | - |\n63-| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given the phase diff, When added comment lines are searched for a spec path or an id, Then nothing is found and only seven files changed | Observed: the comment id search in `scratch/boundaries.txt` exited 1 and the AGENTS.md and package checks printed nothing. Eight files changed, the seven named plus `command-routing-baseline.json`, recaptured under decision P020 in `../decision-record.md` (`tasks.md:110`) | Met | - |\n64-| AC-009 | REQ-001 | Given the whole advisor suite, When it runs after the build, Then it reports 0 failed with more passed tests than before | Observed: `scratch/after.txt` holds 1919 passed, 6 skipped and 0 failed over 184 of 184 files, against 1838 passed before (`tasks.md:107`) | Met | - |\n65-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards && sed -n '118,124p;180,188p' spec.md | cat -n | cut -c1-700; echo \\\"--- AC-007\\\"; rg -n \\\"AC-007\\\" -A3 acceptance-criteria.md | cut -c1-600\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681055688,"end":1794681057800}}}}
