{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681118260,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db54959d002DbmVhn2pEMLXtv","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db545927001dsxdl5urFdf2Gn","type":"tool","id":"call_236d9981591d41669cdb2b9f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation && rg -n \"T004|T005|T014|T015|T016|T017\" tasks.md | rg \"^\\d+:-\" | cut -c1-900"},"output":"79:- [x] T004 [P] Carry a decline lead over an or-list (`CAT`, then `CA` new constant `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and its one use in `commandOnlyMentioned`). After T003. Test first: in `CAT`, inside `describe('a command the prompt only mentions')`, add `it.each([['do not run /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['never use /create:readme or /create:feature-catalog', '/create:feature-catalog'], ['do not run /deep:review, or /deep:research', '/deep:research'], ['skip /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['do not run /speckit:plan or /speckit:implement or /speckit:complete', '/speckit:complete']])('reads %s as a refusal of %s through an or-list', ...)` expecting `true`, and `it.each([['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:agent'], ['use /create:agent or /create:readme', '/create:readme'], ['use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete', '/speckit:plan'], ['do not\n80:- [x] T005 Read the article after a bare ask word (`CAT`, then `CA` constant `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD`). After T004. This task changes that one constant and its comment. Test first: in `CAT`, add the row `['Is the /doctor:update command safe?', '/doctor:update']` to the table of the case `reads %s as a question about %s`, and the row `['the next step is the /speckit:implement command', '/speckit:implement']` to the table that holds `the next step is /speckit:implement`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first row return `false` while the second passes. Then change `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` to `'(?:is|does|can|will|would) (?:the )?'` and add one sentence to the comment above it: a question often names the command after `the`, as in `is the /x command safe`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `\n107:- [x] T014 [P] Say that the head keeps its command (`FA`). After T003. Replace the sentence that starts ``A hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result`` and the sentence after it with: ``A hub below the head leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row, because `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered. The head keeps its command even then, because every caller renders the head and at most one partner.`` Verify: `rg -c -F 'The head keeps its command even then' $FA` prints 1, `rg -c -F 'A hub below the head leaves' $FA` prints 1, and `rg -n -F 'index === 0' $ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` prints one line. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: exact two-sentence replacement, both rg counts 1, index === 0 at advisor-recommend.ts\n108:- [x] T015 Correct the case count of the meaning anchor test (`FM`). After T014. In the row for `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, replace `17 cases:` with `28 cases:`. Before the edit, run `rg -c -e '^\\s*it\\(' $ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. When it prints another number than 28, write that number in place of 28 and say so in the evidence. Verify: `rg -c -F '28 cases:' $FM` prints 1, or the printed count does, and `rg -c -F '17 cases' $FM` prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS, doc-only: it( count 28, vitest 28 of 28, 28 cases: prints 1, 17 cases prints nothing\n109:- [x] T016 Name the child form on the companion line (`AR`). After 