{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681196271,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db55cc8a002HdmchapnAIXMEc","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db55b7fd0018cxe30bH6kVTzo","type":"tool","id":"call_778757d02dc546a2a1caa276","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-223\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-confirm-4b lineage\n3: description: Runtime strategy tracking the confirming round of review pass four for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage.\n4: version: 1.11.14.0\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-confirm-4b lineage\n8: \n9: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n10: \n11: ### Purpose\n12: \n13: Persistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n14: (P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\n15: iteration before any review action.\n16: \n17: ### Ownership\n18: \n19: Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\n20: commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. TOPIC\n25: \n26: Confirming round of review pass four of\n27: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` in the\n28: `scorer-attach` area, over the fix commit range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`.\n29: \n30: Scope: the `scorer-attach` area rows of `review/review-scope-4b.txt` — `command-attach.ts`,\n31: `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, the four matching tests, and the shared docs that describe\n32: them (`README.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`,\n33: `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`). The `accuracy-runner` rows\n34: (`codex.mjs`, `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, their tests and the doctor\n35: presentation asset) belong to the sibling lineage and are read here only as context.\n36: \n37: This round confirms the fixes for the findings in `review/verify-4/report.md` and looks for\n38: defects those fixes added. A finding the report rejects or records as an accepted limit is not\n39: re-raised without a new input that breaks it.\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n44: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n45: - [ ] security\n46: - [ ] traceability\n47: - [ ] maintainability\n48: \n49: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n54: \n55: - The accuracy-runner harness and session readers are the sibling lineage's code scope; this\n56:   lineage checks only that its own scoring surface agrees with them.\n57: - Hook, plugin, render and doctor-command code is outside both scope rows.\n58: - Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n59:   `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n60: - No code changes: review is observation-only.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n65: \n66: - Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold.\n67: - Cap: `maxIterations` 3; the terminal record must carry `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\n68: - Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n69: - Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n74: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n75: - [x] correctness\n76: \n77: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n82: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n83: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n84: - P1 (Required): 1\n85: - P2 (Suggestions): 3\n86: - Resolved: 0\n87: \n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 8. WHAT WORKE