{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681251608,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db562adf0011iLCUWVuaxRLO3","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db5616de0012iVudGoggwNLbQ","type":"tool","id":"call_a3110ce0072443cfaf6eeb59","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002 — scorer-attach-confirm-4b\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review, fan-out lineage)\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach-confirm-4b`, session `fanout-scorer-attach-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Focus: traceability — the remediation plan's own contract for each fix, packet-doc claims, and the doc rows\n- Operator focus: `review-brief-4b.txt` — confirming round of pass four. This iteration addressed it by reading the remediation spec that owns each fix (`027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`, `tasks.md`), mapping every scorer-attach row to its task and verification line, and correcting one iteration-1 finding whose evidence came from a ripgrep replacement artifact rather than the file.\n- Sources read: `steer.md` (absent), `review-brief-4b.txt`, `review-scope-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` (finding table, P046/P048, A6), `027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md` (T004, T005, T014-T017, CHK-FIX-001, CHK-FIX-004), `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md` (REQ-003, edge cases), `runtime/lib/render.ts`, `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`.\n- Budget profile: verify (10 analysis calls).\n\n## Corrections\n\n1. **SAC4B-P2-002 is retracted.** Iteration 1 reported that `README.md:121` names `parent-named only` while the renderer prints `(n)`. The evidence came from `rg -rn \"parent-named only\"`, where `-r` is ripgrep's *replace* flag: the printed `n` was my own replacement text, not file content. Re-read without `-r`: `render.ts:113` is `const PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only';`, `render.ts:48` says \"renders as parent-named only\", and `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84` asserts `... /doctor:update (parent-named only)`. The README sentence is correct and matches the code; 027 T016's verification line (`tasks.md:109`) also checks that exact constant. Withdrawn from the registry via `resolvedFindings`.\n2. **`iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field` is an accepted deferral, not an unfixed finding.** `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:214` records it with the pair-block and `paired` name as deferred to phase 026 T052 (operator decision P046). It remains a dead field (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1633,1702`, no increment path), but the remediation plan owns it. Closed here as deferred, not re-raised.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:195-215,380-390`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:79-80,107-110,218,221,246`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md:175,241`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:48,113,204-216`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:366-440` (re-read for the contract comparison)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-201` (re-read)\n\nContext-only (sibling rows): `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:69,124,188`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. **SAC4B-P1-001 remains active and is strengthened, not re-raised:** `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:201` states the fix contract for SA4-P1-002 as \"A decline lead also covers every command an or-list joins to the one it leads.\" The implementation at `command-attach.ts:379` joins only `/cmd or /cmd`, so `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still returns a command (probe, iteration 1). The contract names the command the list joins, not the literal absence of the article, so the article form is inside the fix's own promise. The missing test row is visible against `027 tasks.md:79` (all five rows are bare forms), while `CHK-FIX-004` (`tasks.md:221`) asks for the delimiter and joined-input cases; the article form is a delimiter-adjacent case with no row.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` — remediation contract per scorer-attach fix | partial | T004 (`027/spec.md:201`), T009 (`:205`), docs T014-T016 (`:209`, `tasks.md:107-109`) all match their code; T004's contract is met only for the bare or-list form (SAC4B-P1-001) |\n| `checklist_evidence` — CHK-FIX-001, CHK-FIX-004, CHK-042 | pass with one gap | finding classes and doc corrections hold (`tasks.md:218,246`); CHK-FIX-004's adversarial table has no article-inside-or-list row (`tasks.md:221`) |\n| `skill_agent` — README describes the skill's own behaviour | pass | `README.md:121` matches `render.ts:113` and `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84` (correction 1) |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` — sibling-owned Codex reader | pass (context) | `codex.mjs:164-171` opens `storePath`; not this lineage's row |\n| `feature_catalog_code` — feature-catalog rows | pass | `advisor-recommend.md:39` ↔ `advisor-recommend.ts:475-478`; `command-meaning-matching.md:65` ↔ 28 `it` blocks (027 T015, `tasks.md:108`) |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | no playbook in scope |\n| 020 REQ-003 reach | pass as written, silent on the article | `020/spec.md:175` names the seven prompts; `020/spec.md:241` says a two-command prompt is read once per command, which the article form still satisfies semantically while the code returns a request |\n| Accepted limits not re-raised | pass | SA4-P1-001 (retired name) and SA4-P1-003 (broad creation words) accepted at `027/spec.md:199-200`; SA4-P2-004 superseded by note at `027/spec.md:210` (P048); unscoredOnly/pair/paired deferred at `:214` (P046) |\n\nCore protocol status after this iteration: `spec_code` partial (one open contract gap, SAC4B-P1-001), `checklist_evidence` pass with the same gap. Dimension covered: traceability.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Remediation ownership: `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` is the packet doc that names each fix, its finding class (CHK-FIX-001) and its deferral decisions (P046, P048); it is the traceability anchor for this round.\n- Documentation chain: `README.md:121` → `render.ts:113` → `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84` all agree on the child-session policy phrase.\n- Sibling boundary: `routing-accuracy/README.md` carries the `offeredAs`, pair-block and A11 rows; those are accuracy-runner rows and are not raised here.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The retraction in this iteration changes the running P2 count from 3 to 1 (SAC4B-P2-001 only). The registry now records the closed id and the deferred id; the narrative and delta agree.\n- `rg -r` is a destructive read habit in a review: it prints the file as if edited. Every finding in this lineage is now either probe-verified (module import) or `rg -n`-verified; no finding rests on a `-r` output.\n- `SA4-P2-004` (phase 020 says 10, code uses 9) is a superseding note, not an erratum, by operator decision P048 (`027/spec.md:210,387`); not raised.\n- The article-inside-or-list gap has no test row; the fix's own task list (T004) defines only the bare form, so a follow-up fix must widen both the constant and the table.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` article fix matches its task exactly (`027 tasks.md:80`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:198`).\n- Meaning-anchor count 28 matches the doc row and 027 T015's verification (`tasks.md:108`).\n- Head-keeps-command sentence matches `index === 0` (`advisor-recommend.md:39`, `advisor-recommend.ts:478`).\n- Shell-read start and heredoc end-word fixes map to 027 T009/T010 (`027/spec.md:205`) and their task rows.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- `R4-P2-002`, `iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated`, `iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned`: rejected in `verify-4/report.md`; no new input found.\n- `SA4-P2-004` (10 vs 9): accepted superseding note under P048; re-reporting it would contradict the operator decision.\n- `iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows`, `iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision`, `iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field`: accepted deferrals to phase 026 (P046); not re-raised.\n- The 027 T016 verification line was re-run mentally against the real file: `rg -c -F \"PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only'\" render.ts` prints 1, so the task's evidence is sound. No finding.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (combined pass)\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene in the scorer's live capture path, guard reach and regex cost on the new or-list constant, dead code and test pinning on the new rows\n- Reason: traceability is complete and the remaining configured dimensions have no iteration of coverage; the convergence gate needs both before STOP\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability remaining\n- Required evidence: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` holdout path (`:1201-1240,1500-1520`), `COMMAND_OR_LIST` cost and reach, the three new test tables\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002 — scorer-attach-confirm-4b\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review, fan-out lineage)\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach-confirm-4b`, session `fanout-scorer-attach-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Focus: traceability — the remediation plan's own contract for each fix, packet-doc claims, and the doc rows\\n- Operator focus: `review-brief-4b.txt` — confirming round of pass four. This iteration addressed it by reading the remediation spec that owns each fix (`027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md`, `tasks.md`), mapping every scorer-attach row to its task and verification line, and correcting one iteration-1 finding whose evidence came from a ripgrep replacement artifact rather than the file.\\n- Sources read: `steer.md` (absent), `review-brief-4b.txt`, `review-scope-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` (finding table, P046/P048, A6), `027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md` (T004, T005, T014-T017, CHK-FIX-001, CHK-FIX-004), `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md` (REQ-003, edge cases), `runtime/lib/render.ts`, `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`.\\n- Budget profile: verify (10 analysis calls).\\n\\n## Corrections\\n\\n1. **SAC4B-P2-002 is retracted.** Iteration 1 reported that `README.md:121` names `parent-named only` while the renderer prints `(n)`. The evidence came from `rg -rn \\\"parent-named only\\\"`, where `-r` is ripgrep's *replace* flag: the printed `n` was my own replacement text, not file content. Re-read without `-r`: `render.ts:113` is `const PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only';`, `render.ts:48` says \\\"renders as parent-named only\\\", and `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84` asserts `... /doctor:update (parent-named only)`. The README sentence is correct and matches the code; 027 T016's verification line (`tasks.md:109`) also checks that exact constant. Withdrawn from the registry via `resolvedFindings`.\\n2. **`iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field` is an accepted deferral, not an unfixed finding.** `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:214` records it with the pair-block and `paired` name as deferred to phase 026 T052 (operator decision P046). It remains a dead field (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1633,1702`, no increment path), but the remediation plan owns it. Closed here as deferred, not re-raised.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:195-215,380-390`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/tasks.md:79-80,107-110,218,221,246`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md:175,241`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:48,113,204-216`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:366-440` (re-read for the contract comparison)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-201` (re-read)\\n\\nContext-only (sibling rows): `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:69,124,188`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. **SAC4B-P1-001 remains active and is strengthened, not re-raised:** `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:201` states the fix contract for SA4-P1-002 as \\\"A decline lead also covers every command an or-list joins to the one it leads.\\\" The implementation at `command-attach.ts:379` joins only `/cmd or /cmd`, so `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` still returns a command (probe, iteration 1). The contract names the command the list joins, not the literal absence of the article, so the article form is inside the fix's own promise. The missing test row is visible against `027 tasks.md:79` (all five rows are bare forms), while `CHK-FIX-004` (`tasks.md:221`) asks for the delimiter and joined-input cases; the article form is a delimiter-adjacent case with no row.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` — remediation contract per scorer-attach fix | partial | T004 (`027/spec.md:201`), T009 (`:205`), docs T014-T016 (`:209`, `tasks.md:107-109`) all match their code; T004's contract is met only for the bare or-list form (SAC4B-P1-001) |\\n| `checklist_evidence` — CHK-FIX-001, CHK-FIX-004, CHK-042 | pass with one gap | finding classes and doc corrections hold (`tasks.md:218,246`); CHK-FIX-004's adversarial table has no article-inside-or-list row (`tasks.md:221`) |\\n| `skill_agent` — README describes the skill's own behaviour | pass | `README.md:121` matches `render.ts:113` and `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84` (correction 1) |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` — sibling-owned Codex reader | pass (context) | `codex.mjs:164-171` opens `storePath`; not this lineage's row |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` — feature-catalog rows | pass | `advisor-recommend.md:39` ↔ `advisor-recommend.ts:475-478`; `command-meaning-matching.md:65` ↔ 28 `it` blocks (027 T015, `tasks.md:108`) |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | no playbook in scope |\\n| 020 REQ-003 reach | pass as written, silent on the article | `020/spec.md:175` names the seven prompts; `020/spec.md:241` says a two-command prompt is read once per command, which the article form still satisfies semantically while the code returns a request |\\n| Accepted limits not re-raised | pass | SA4-P1-001 (retired name) and SA4-P1-003 (broad creation words) accepted at `027/spec.md:199-200`; SA4-P2-004 superseded by note at `027/spec.md:210` (P048); unscoredOnly/pair/paired deferred at `:214` (P046) |\\n\\nCore protocol status after this iteration: `spec_code` partial (one open contract gap, SAC4B-P1-001), `checklist_evidence` pass with the same gap. Dimension covered: traceability.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Remediation ownership: `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` is the packet doc that names each fix, its finding class (CHK-FIX-001) and its deferral decisions (P046, P048); it is the traceability anchor for this round.\\n- Documentation chain: `README.md:121` → `render.ts:113` → `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84` all agree on the child-session policy phrase.\\n- Sibling boundary: `routing-accuracy/README.md` carries the `offeredAs`, pair-block and A11 rows; those are accuracy-runner rows and are not raised here.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The retraction in this iteration changes the running P2 count from 3 to 1 (SAC4B-P2-001 only). The registry now records the closed id and the deferred id; the narrative and delta agree.\\n- `rg -r` is a destructive read habit in a review: it prints the file as if edited. Every finding in this lineage is now either probe-verified (module import) or `rg -n`-verified; no finding rests on a `-r` output.\\n- `SA4-P2-004` (phase 020 says 10, code uses 9) is a superseding note, not an erratum, by operator decision P048 (`027/spec.md:210,387`); not raised.\\n- The article-inside-or-list gap has no test row; the fix's own task list (T004) defines only the bare form, so a follow-up fix must widen both the constant and the table.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` article fix matches its task exactly (`027 tasks.md:80`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:198`).\\n- Meaning-anchor count 28 matches the doc row and 027 T015's verification (`tasks.md:108`).\\n- Head-keeps-command sentence matches `index === 0` (`advisor-recommend.md:39`, `advisor-recommend.ts:478`).\\n- Shell-read start and heredoc end-word fixes map to 027 T009/T010 (`027/spec.md:205`) and their task rows.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- `R4-P2-002`, `iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated`, `iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned`: rejected in `verify-4/report.md`; no new input found.\\n- `SA4-P2-004` (10 vs 9): accepted superseding note under P048; re-reporting it would contradict the operator decision.\\n- `iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows`, `iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision`, `iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field`: accepted deferrals to phase 026 (P046); not re-raised.\\n- The 027 T016 verification line was re-run mentally against the real file: `rg -c -F \\\"PARENT_NAMED_POLICY = 'parent-named only'\\\" render.ts` prints 1, so the task's evidence is sound. No finding.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security and maintainability (combined pass)\\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene in the scorer's live capture path, guard reach and regex cost on the new or-list constant, dead code and test pinning on the new rows\\n- Reason: traceability is complete and the remaining configured dimensions have no iteration of coverage; the convergence gate needs both before STOP\\n- Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability remaining\\n- Required evidence: `score-command-transcripts.mjs` holdout path (`:1201-1240,1500-1520`), `COMMAND_OR_LIST` cost and reach, the three new test tables\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681219807,"end":1794681251608}}}}
