{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681506283,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db5a3161001YNP74rwkmZdpn8","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db59fa1e00107in9s36p7IM7r","type":"tool","id":"call_3a9313bf92934de3986b3617","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003 — scorer-attach-confirm-4b\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (deep-review, fan-out lineage)\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach-confirm-4b`, session `fanout-scorer-attach-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\n- Focus: security and maintainability (combined pass)\n- Operator focus: `review-brief-4b.txt` — confirming round of pass four. This iteration addressed it by taking the two checks not yet covered by a dimension: holdout hygiene in the scorer that reads the capture, and the cost, comment hygiene and test pinning of the two new matching constructs.\n- Sources read: `steer.md` (absent), `review-brief-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (row-label load, `scoreRun`, `shellReadTargets`, `readDocument`), `command-attach.ts` (new constants and the mention reader), the three new test tables, and the added comment lines in the fix diff.\n- Budget profile: verify (9 analysis calls).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1198-1245,1500-1518,638-694,910-925`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:373-395,411-440`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-201`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:614-640,1082-1120,2279-2284`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:129-230`\n- Fix-diff added comment lines for id hygiene (both core files)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. Both active findings are carried from iteration 1: SAC4B-P1-001 (or-list article form) and SAC4B-P2-001 (question over an or-list).\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Security Checks\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Holdout rows never open a session or print a prompt | pass | `loadRowLabels` stores only `{holdout:true}` for a holdout split (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1236`); `scoreRun` returns `{scored:false, reason:'holdout_row'}` before `loadSession` (`:1510`) |\n| Holdout guard reads the live capture | pass | `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:205-215` asserts on `live` for all four published maps, plus a map-level test at `:216-231` |\n| No prompt text reaches an output line through the new code | pass | the shell-read branch only inspects `event.command` (`:921`); no label or prompt field is read there |\n| Untrusted input in the new regexes cannot execute or open a path | pass | `COMMAND_OR_LIST` is a pure character-class alternation (`command-attach.ts:379`); `shellReadTargets` only splits a string and compares tails, no filesystem call |\n| Regex cost of the or-list | pass | timed on a 10/100/400/1200-item list: 0.18 ms or less per full match (`node` probe, iteration 3); each repetition consumes at least one `/`, so no empty-iteration backtracking |\n| Trust-boundary reach unchanged | pass | the new branches widen only what counts as a read; they add no new input source |\n\n## Maintainability Checks\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Comment hygiene (no spec/phase/task/finding ids) | pass | added lines in both files carry no `0NN-`, `T0NN`, `P0NN`, `SA4`, `REQ-` or `AC-` token (`git diff … | grep '^+' | rg` returns nothing) |\n| Comments name the durable why | pass | `command-attach.ts:376-379` explains why the list joins only `or`/`, or`; `:394` explains the article; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:646-648,914-916` explain the end-word class and the shell-read rule |\n| New test rows pin the fixed behaviour | partial | the five or-list rows, the is-the row, the shell-read table and both heredoc rows pin their fixes; the article-inside-or-list form has no row (SAC4B-P1-001) |\n| No new dead code | pass | every new constant is used once (`COMMAND_OR_LIST`, `publishedHoldoutIds`); no unused export |\n| Test helper shape | pass | `publishedHoldoutIds` is a local helper over the same four maps the inline check read; the second test makes the helper's own coverage explicit rather than relying on a case that happens to hit one map |\n| Repo-rule id hygiene on docs | pass | all three doc edits are prose plus a version bump; no id is embedded |\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | unchanged partial | carries SAC4B-P1-001; nothing in this iteration changes the spec-side reach judgment |\n| `checklist_evidence` | unchanged partial | same gap; no new checklist row |\n| `skill_agent` / `feature_catalog_code` | pass | iteration 2 result holds |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass (context) | Codex reader is sibling-owned and verified |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The holdout rule and the `publishedHoldoutIds` helper run inside the same vitest file that scores the corpus, so the guard cannot be bypassed by a different capture writer without failing the suite.\n- The shell-read branch is reached from both `startState` (`:986`) and `takenLoop` (`:1439`) through the one `readDocument`, so no second copy of the rule can drift.\n- The or-list constant is consumed by the same `commandOnlyMentioned` that `attachCommand` (`:491`) and the typed path call, so the P1 fix location is the shared reader, not a caller.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A failed shell read (`cat` exiting non-zero) still counts as a start because the normalized event carries no exit code. This is unchanged by the fix and outside its claim; recorded, not raised.\n- `{holdout:true}` replaces the label object entirely, so a holdout row also loses its expected command in memory — a safe default that keeps a future field from leaking through.\n- The 1200-item timing probe is a synthetic worst case for the delimiter, not a real prompt; it establishes no super-linear blowup, nothing more.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `scoreRun` holdout gate ordering (label → holdout → session load).\n- `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` comment accuracy against behaviour.\n- New test tables: or-list refusals, request controls, is-the question, shell-read start, heredoc end words.\n- No id leakage in any added comment line.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- ReDoS on `COMMAND_OR_LIST`: the repetition cannot match empty, so the `$` anchor cannot force exponential backtracking; measured flat.\n- Holdout leak through `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`: the live capture is now checked; no prompt value is read by the helper.\n- `unscoredOnly`, pair-block and `paired` name: accepted deferrals to phase 026 (P046), not re-raised.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining\n- Focus area: synthesis\n- Reason: correctness, traceability, security and maintainability each have one full iteration; the last two produced no new findings\n- Rotation status: all dimensions covered\n- Required evidence: `verify-4/report.md` ledger plus iterations 1-3\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003 — scorer-attach-confirm-4b\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (deep-review, fan-out lineage)\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach-confirm-4b`, session `fanout-scorer-attach-confirm-4b-1794680176420-xvj4ed`, generation 1, lineageMode `new`\\n- Focus: security and maintainability (combined pass)\\n- Operator focus: `review-brief-4b.txt` — confirming round of pass four. This iteration addressed it by taking the two checks not yet covered by a dimension: holdout hygiene in the scorer that reads the capture, and the cost, comment hygiene and test pinning of the two new matching constructs.\\n- Sources read: `steer.md` (absent), `review-brief-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (row-label load, `scoreRun`, `shellReadTargets`, `readDocument`), `command-attach.ts` (new constants and the mention reader), the three new test tables, and the added comment lines in the fix diff.\\n- Budget profile: verify (9 analysis calls).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1198-1245,1500-1518,638-694,910-925`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:373-395,411-440`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-201`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:614-640,1082-1120,2279-2284`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:129-230`\\n- Fix-diff added comment lines for id hygiene (both core files)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Both active findings are carried from iteration 1: SAC4B-P1-001 (or-list article form) and SAC4B-P2-001 (question over an or-list).\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new.\\n\\n## Security Checks\\n\\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Holdout rows never open a session or print a prompt | pass | `loadRowLabels` stores only `{holdout:true}` for a holdout split (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1236`); `scoreRun` returns `{scored:false, reason:'holdout_row'}` before `loadSession` (`:1510`) |\\n| Holdout guard reads the live capture | pass | `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:205-215` asserts on `live` for all four published maps, plus a map-level test at `:216-231` |\\n| No prompt text reaches an output line through the new code | pass | the shell-read branch only inspects `event.command` (`:921`); no label or prompt field is read there |\\n| Untrusted input in the new regexes cannot execute or open a path | pass | `COMMAND_OR_LIST` is a pure character-class alternation (`command-attach.ts:379`); `shellReadTargets` only splits a string and compares tails, no filesystem call |\\n| Regex cost of the or-list | pass | timed on a 10/100/400/1200-item list: 0.18 ms or less per full match (`node` probe, iteration 3); each repetition consumes at least one `/`, so no empty-iteration backtracking |\\n| Trust-boundary reach unchanged | pass | the new branches widen only what counts as a read; they add no new input source |\\n\\n## Maintainability Checks\\n\\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Comment hygiene (no spec/phase/task/finding ids) | pass | added lines in both files carry no `0NN-`, `T0NN`, `P0NN`, `SA4`, `REQ-` or `AC-` token (`git diff … | grep '^+' | rg` returns nothing) |\\n| Comments name the durable why | pass | `command-attach.ts:376-379` explains why the list joins only `or`/`, or`; `:394` explains the article; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:646-648,914-916` explain the end-word class and the shell-read rule |\\n| New test rows pin the fixed behaviour | partial | the five or-list rows, the is-the row, the shell-read table and both heredoc rows pin their fixes; the article-inside-or-list form has no row (SAC4B-P1-001) |\\n| No new dead code | pass | every new constant is used once (`COMMAND_OR_LIST`, `publishedHoldoutIds`); no unused export |\\n| Test helper shape | pass | `publishedHoldoutIds` is a local helper over the same four maps the inline check read; the second test makes the helper's own coverage explicit rather than relying on a case that happens to hit one map |\\n| Repo-rule id hygiene on docs | pass | all three doc edits are prose plus a version bump; no id is embedded |\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Check | Result | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | unchanged partial | carries SAC4B-P1-001; nothing in this iteration changes the spec-side reach judgment |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | unchanged partial | same gap; no new checklist row |\\n| `skill_agent` / `feature_catalog_code` | pass | iteration 2 result holds |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | pass (context) | Codex reader is sibling-owned and verified |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The holdout rule and the `publishedHoldoutIds` helper run inside the same vitest file that scores the corpus, so the guard cannot be bypassed by a different capture writer without failing the suite.\\n- The shell-read branch is reached from both `startState` (`:986`) and `takenLoop` (`:1439`) through the one `readDocument`, so no second copy of the rule can drift.\\n- The or-list constant is consumed by the same `commandOnlyMentioned` that `attachCommand` (`:491`) and the typed path call, so the P1 fix location is the shared reader, not a caller.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A failed shell read (`cat` exiting non-zero) still counts as a start because the normalized event carries no exit code. This is unchanged by the fix and outside its claim; recorded, not raised.\\n- `{holdout:true}` replaces the label object entirely, so a holdout row also loses its expected command in memory — a safe default that keeps a future field from leaking through.\\n- The 1200-item timing probe is a synthetic worst case for the delimiter, not a real prompt; it establishes no super-linear blowup, nothing more.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `scoreRun` holdout gate ordering (label → holdout → session load).\\n- `COMMAND_OR_LIST` and `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` comment accuracy against behaviour.\\n- New test tables: or-list refusals, request controls, is-the question, shell-read start, heredoc end words.\\n- No id leakage in any added comment line.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- ReDoS on `COMMAND_OR_LIST`: the repetition cannot match empty, so the `$` anchor cannot force exponential backtracking; measured flat.\\n- Holdout leak through `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`: the live capture is now checked; no prompt value is read by the helper.\\n- `unscoredOnly`, pair-block and `paired` name: accepted deferrals to phase 026 (P046), not re-raised.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining\\n- Focus area: synthesis\\n- Reason: correctness, traceability, security and maintainability each have one full iteration; the last two produced no new findings\\n- Rotation status: all dimensions covered\\n- Required evidence: `verify-4/report.md` ledger plus iterations 1-3\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681483617,"end":1794681506283}}}}
