{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794681624368,"sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","part":{"partID":"prt_1db5bdddc001kKiA1Uj6vapw7i","sessionID":"ses_e24b9ad87ffe4Yqg6PDGQGxiHx","messageID":"msg_1db5bd5d2001GmNzHeNlm9ad9z","type":"tool","id":"call_36de11682b2548fb947d7404","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report — scorer-attach-confirm-4b\n\nLineage `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` of the command-surfacing pass-four confirming round.\nTarget: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\nRange: `11af224a34..48f03b5013`. Scope rows: the `scorer-attach` area of `review/review-scope-4b.txt`.\nLedger: `review/verify-4/report.md`; brief: `review/review-brief-4b.txt`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- Overall verdict: **CONDITIONAL**\n- hasAdvisories: false (a P1 is active, so the verdict is not PASS)\n- Active counts: P0 0, P1 1, P2 1\n- Review scope: eight files — the attach reader, the transcript scorer, three test files, and three shared docs\n- Operator review focus: Confirming round of review pass four of command surfacing. Scope: `review-scope-4b.txt` lists the files of the fix commit, one per line as area TAB path, for the commit range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`. This lineage reviews the lines whose area is `scorer-attach`, plus the shared docs that describe them. The round confirms the fixes for the findings in `review/verify-4/report.md` and looks for defects the fixes added. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. The holdout rule held throughout: `command-prompts.jsonl` and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` were never opened except through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`, no diff over a path including `command-prompts.jsonl` ran without the exclude pathspec, and no holdout prompt was printed.\n\nThe round confirms eight of the nine fixes in its scope and finds one incomplete fix: the or-list refusal reader joins only `or /cmd`, so a refusal that names its second command as `or the /cmd command` still yields a command. One earlier finding was retracted after re-reading its evidence, and one was closed as an operator-approved deferral.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required: one active P1 remains.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\"SAC4B-P1-001\", \"SAC4B-P2-001\"],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    \"Widen COMMAND_OR_LIST to accept the article before a joined command and add one refusal row per widened form\",\n    \"Apply the same list rule to COMMAND_ASK_LEADS and pin a question-over-a-list row\"\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"The or-list refusal contract in the pass-four remediation spec covers every command the list joins; name the article form explicitly\",\n    \"The question branch shares the refusal grammar's list rule; say so in the same sentence\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Edit the one constant and its two use sites, test-first with the article input\",\n    \"Add the article row to the adversarial delimiter table\",\n    \"Re-run command-attach-guards and the attach slice\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": {\n    \"SAC4B-P1-001\": \"class-of-bug\",\n    \"SAC4B-P2-001\": \"class-of-bug\"\n  },\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"commandOnlyMentioned\",\n    \"attachCommand\",\n    \"refusal lead grammar\",\n    \"COMMAND_ASK_LEADS\",\n    \"or-list\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n### SAC4B-P1-001 — P1, correctness\n\n- Title: An or-list refusal that names its second command as \"the /x command\" still attaches that command\n- Location: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:379` (constant), `:425-426` (decline branch), `:491` (attach gate), `:512` (return)\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_OR_LIST` is `(?:\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?,? or )*`, so the joined item must start at `/`. A module-level probe printed `REQUEST` for `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command`, `skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command` and `do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command`, while `do not run /create:agent or /create:readme` printed `MENTION`.\n- Impact: a refusal can still carry a `(start)`-policy command, the harm class the pass-four fix set out to close.\n- Fix recommendation: make the joined item `(?:the )?` tolerant inside `COMMAND_OR_LIST` (one constant plus its test row), and confirm a second use verb still opens a new clause.\n- Disposition: open\n- Finding class: class-of-bug\n- Scope proof: the constant has one use; the five or-list rows in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-163` all use the bare form, and `027 tasks.md:79` defines only that form.\n- Affected surface hints: `commandOnlyMentioned`, `attachCommand`, `refusal lead grammar`, `or-list`\n\n### SAC4B-P2-001 — P2, correctness\n\n- Title: A question over an or-list still attaches its second command\n- Location: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:386-389`\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` never receives `COMMAND_OR_LIST`; the probe printed `REQUEST` for `what does /create:readme or /create:agent do?` against `/create:agent`, while the single-command question printed `MENTION`.\n- Impact: a pure question can carry a mutating command; advisory because the brief scoped the or-list fix to refusals.\n- Fix recommendation: share the list rule between the decline and ask branches.\n- Disposition: open\n- Finding class: class-of-bug\n- Scope proof: one pattern family; no ask-side list row exists in the guard table.\n- Affected surface hints: `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS`, `commandOnlyMentioned`\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **P1 — close the or-list grammar gap.** Edit `COMMAND_OR_LIST`, add the article row, and re-run `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` plus the attach slice.\n2. **P2 — share the list rule with the ask branch.** Apply the same constant in `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` and add one question-over-a-list row.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The pass-four remediation spec already states that a decline lead covers every command an or-list joins; make the article form explicit so the fix and its test row cannot diverge again.\n- The question branch is the same grammar over a different lead family; state the shared rule once.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Test-first: add `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` to the refusal table and watch it fail.\n- Widen the constant, keep `do not run A or run B` as the request control.\n- Add the ask-side row and apply the constant.\n- Re-run the guard table and the attach slice; no stored score moves (the gate feeds offers, not the corpus numbers).\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n- `spec_code`: **partial** — the pass-four remediation contract for the or-list (`027/spec.md:201`) is met for the bare form only; the article form stays a request. The live-holdout, shell-read, heredoc, head-command and doc tasks (T006-T016) match their code.\n- `checklist_evidence`: **partial** — CHK-FIX-004's adversarial delimiter table (`027/tasks.md:221`) has no article-inside-or-list row; every other required row holds.\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n- `skill_agent`: **pass** — `README.md:121` matches `render.ts:113` and `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84`.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: **pass (context)** — the Codex reader opens the containment-resolved `storePath` (`codex.mjs:164-171`); sibling-owned.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: **pass** — `advisor-recommend.md:39` matches `advisor-recommend.ts:475-478`; `command-meaning-matching.md:65` matches 28 test blocks.\n- `playbook_capability`: **notApplicable** — no playbook in scope.\n\n### AC_COVERAGE\n\n`exempt` — this lineage reviews the pass-four fix rows, not packet closure; no ACC coverage signal was computed and the advisory signal does not alter the verdict.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- `iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field` (dead `unscoredOnly` in the summary projection): operator decision P046 defers it to phase 026 T052. Confirmed still dead, not counted active.\n- `iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows` and `iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision`: same deferral to phase 026 (P046).\n- `SA4-P1-001` (retired name in a refusal) and `SA4-P1-003` (broad creation words): accepted limits under P045, not built.\n- `SA4-P2-004` (phase 020 says 10, code uses 9): superseding note under P048.\n\n## 9. Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Selected review directions: correctness (iteration 1) → traceability (iteration 2) → security and maintainability (iteration 3)\n- Saturated directions: none\n- Remaining frontier: none\n\n## 10. Search Ledger\n\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record).*\n\n## 11. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence\n\n- Iterations: 3 of 3 (cap reached; the third produced no new findings and all dimensions are covered)\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`\n- newFindingsRatio by iteration: 1 → 0.88, 2 → 0, 3 → 0\n- Active findings: P0 0, P1 1, P2 1\n\n### Coverage\n\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, traceability, security, maintainability (4 of 4)\n- Files reviewed: `command-attach.ts`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `README.md`, `advisor-recommend.md`, `command-meaning-matching.md`\n\n### Ruled Out Claims\n\n- `R4-P2-002` first-row lead, `iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated`, `iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned`: rejected by the verifier; no new input found.\n- ReDoS on `COMMAND_OR_LIST`: flat timing to 1200 list items; the repetition cannot match empty.\n- Holdout leak through the live capture: guarded on all four published maps.\n- `unscoredOnly` as active work: deferred by P046.\n\n### Corrections\n\n- `SAC4B-P2-002` was retracted in iteration 2. Iteration 1 read `render.ts` through `rg -r`, whose replace flag printed the file as if the phrase were `n`; the file prints `parent-named only` and the README matches it.\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n`review-brief-4b.txt`, `review-scope-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` and `tasks.md`, `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md`, the eight scope files, `render.ts`, `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`, `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `codex.mjs`.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report — scorer-attach-confirm-4b\\n\\nLineage `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` of the command-surfacing pass-four confirming round.\\nTarget: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\\nRange: `11af224a34..48f03b5013`. Scope rows: the `scorer-attach` area of `review/review-scope-4b.txt`.\\nLedger: `review/verify-4/report.md`; brief: `review/review-brief-4b.txt`.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- Overall verdict: **CONDITIONAL**\\n- hasAdvisories: false (a P1 is active, so the verdict is not PASS)\\n- Active counts: P0 0, P1 1, P2 1\\n- Review scope: eight files — the attach reader, the transcript scorer, three test files, and three shared docs\\n- Operator review focus: Confirming round of review pass four of command surfacing. Scope: `review-scope-4b.txt` lists the files of the fix commit, one per line as area TAB path, for the commit range `11af224a34..48f03b5013`. This lineage reviews the lines whose area is `scorer-attach`, plus the shared docs that describe them. The round confirms the fixes for the findings in `review/verify-4/report.md` and looks for defects the fixes added. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. The holdout rule held throughout: `command-prompts.jsonl` and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` were never opened except through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`, no diff over a path including `command-prompts.jsonl` ran without the exclude pathspec, and no holdout prompt was printed.\\n\\nThe round confirms eight of the nine fixes in its scope and finds one incomplete fix: the or-list refusal reader joins only `or /cmd`, so a refusal that names its second command as `or the /cmd command` still yields a command. One earlier finding was retracted after re-reading its evidence, and one was closed as an operator-approved deferral.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required: one active P1 remains.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\\"SAC4B-P1-001\\\", \\\"SAC4B-P2-001\\\"],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    \\\"Widen COMMAND_OR_LIST to accept the article before a joined command and add one refusal row per widened form\\\",\\n    \\\"Apply the same list rule to COMMAND_ASK_LEADS and pin a question-over-a-list row\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"The or-list refusal contract in the pass-four remediation spec covers every command the list joins; name the article form explicitly\\\",\\n    \\\"The question branch shares the refusal grammar's list rule; say so in the same sentence\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Edit the one constant and its two use sites, test-first with the article input\\\",\\n    \\\"Add the article row to the adversarial delimiter table\\\",\\n    \\\"Re-run command-attach-guards and the attach slice\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": {\\n    \\\"SAC4B-P1-001\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\",\\n    \\\"SAC4B-P2-001\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"commandOnlyMentioned\\\",\\n    \\\"attachCommand\\\",\\n    \\\"refusal lead grammar\\\",\\n    \\\"COMMAND_ASK_LEADS\\\",\\n    \\\"or-list\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n### SAC4B-P1-001 — P1, correctness\\n\\n- Title: An or-list refusal that names its second command as \\\"the /x command\\\" still attaches that command\\n- Location: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:379` (constant), `:425-426` (decline branch), `:491` (attach gate), `:512` (return)\\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_OR_LIST` is `(?:\\\\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(?::[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)?,? or )*`, so the joined item must start at `/`. A module-level probe printed `REQUEST` for `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command`, `skip /create:agent or the /create:readme command` and `do not run /create:agent, or the /create:readme command`, while `do not run /create:agent or /create:readme` printed `MENTION`.\\n- Impact: a refusal can still carry a `(start)`-policy command, the harm class the pass-four fix set out to close.\\n- Fix recommendation: make the joined item `(?:the )?` tolerant inside `COMMAND_OR_LIST` (one constant plus its test row), and confirm a second use verb still opens a new clause.\\n- Disposition: open\\n- Finding class: class-of-bug\\n- Scope proof: the constant has one use; the five or-list rows in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:155-163` all use the bare form, and `027 tasks.md:79` defines only that form.\\n- Affected surface hints: `commandOnlyMentioned`, `attachCommand`, `refusal lead grammar`, `or-list`\\n\\n### SAC4B-P2-001 — P2, correctness\\n\\n- Title: A question over an or-list still attaches its second command\\n- Location: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:386-389`\\n- Evidence: `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` never receives `COMMAND_OR_LIST`; the probe printed `REQUEST` for `what does /create:readme or /create:agent do?` against `/create:agent`, while the single-command question printed `MENTION`.\\n- Impact: a pure question can carry a mutating command; advisory because the brief scoped the or-list fix to refusals.\\n- Fix recommendation: share the list rule between the decline and ask branches.\\n- Disposition: open\\n- Finding class: class-of-bug\\n- Scope proof: one pattern family; no ask-side list row exists in the guard table.\\n- Affected surface hints: `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS`, `commandOnlyMentioned`\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **P1 — close the or-list grammar gap.** Edit `COMMAND_OR_LIST`, add the article row, and re-run `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` plus the attach slice.\\n2. **P2 — share the list rule with the ask branch.** Apply the same constant in `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` and add one question-over-a-list row.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The pass-four remediation spec already states that a decline lead covers every command an or-list joins; make the article form explicit so the fix and its test row cannot diverge again.\\n- The question branch is the same grammar over a different lead family; state the shared rule once.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Test-first: add `['do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command', '/create:readme']` to the refusal table and watch it fail.\\n- Widen the constant, keep `do not run A or run B` as the request control.\\n- Add the ask-side row and apply the constant.\\n- Re-run the guard table and the attach slice; no stored score moves (the gate feeds offers, not the corpus numbers).\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n- `spec_code`: **partial** — the pass-four remediation contract for the or-list (`027/spec.md:201`) is met for the bare form only; the article form stays a request. The live-holdout, shell-read, heredoc, head-command and doc tasks (T006-T016) match their code.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: **partial** — CHK-FIX-004's adversarial delimiter table (`027/tasks.md:221`) has no article-inside-or-list row; every other required row holds.\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n- `skill_agent`: **pass** — `README.md:121` matches `render.ts:113` and `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts:84`.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: **pass (context)** — the Codex reader opens the containment-resolved `storePath` (`codex.mjs:164-171`); sibling-owned.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: **pass** — `advisor-recommend.md:39` matches `advisor-recommend.ts:475-478`; `command-meaning-matching.md:65` matches 28 test blocks.\\n- `playbook_capability`: **notApplicable** — no playbook in scope.\\n\\n### AC_COVERAGE\\n\\n`exempt` — this lineage reviews the pass-four fix rows, not packet closure; no ACC coverage signal was computed and the advisory signal does not alter the verdict.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- `iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field` (dead `unscoredOnly` in the summary projection): operator decision P046 defers it to phase 026 T052. Confirmed still dead, not counted active.\\n- `iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows` and `iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision`: same deferral to phase 026 (P046).\\n- `SA4-P1-001` (retired name in a refusal) and `SA4-P1-003` (broad creation words): accepted limits under P045, not built.\\n- `SA4-P2-004` (phase 020 says 10, code uses 9): superseding note under P048.\\n\\n## 9. Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Selected review directions: correctness (iteration 1) → traceability (iteration 2) → security and maintainability (iteration 3)\\n- Saturated directions: none\\n- Remaining frontier: none\\n\\n## 10. Search Ledger\\n\\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record).*\\n\\n## 11. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence\\n\\n- Iterations: 3 of 3 (cap reached; the third produced no new findings and all dimensions are covered)\\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`\\n- newFindingsRatio by iteration: 1 → 0.88, 2 → 0, 3 → 0\\n- Active findings: P0 0, P1 1, P2 1\\n\\n### Coverage\\n\\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, traceability, security, maintainability (4 of 4)\\n- Files reviewed: `command-attach.ts`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `README.md`, `advisor-recommend.md`, `command-meaning-matching.md`\\n\\n### Ruled Out Claims\\n\\n- `R4-P2-002` first-row lead, `iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated`, `iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned`: rejected by the verifier; no new input found.\\n- ReDoS on `COMMAND_OR_LIST`: flat timing to 1200 list items; the repetition cannot match empty.\\n- Holdout leak through the live capture: guarded on all four published maps.\\n- `unscoredOnly` as active work: deferred by P046.\\n\\n### Corrections\\n\\n- `SAC4B-P2-002` was retracted in iteration 2. Iteration 1 read `render.ts` through `rg -r`, whose replace flag printed the file as if the phrase were `n`; the file prints `parent-named only` and the README matches it.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n`review-brief-4b.txt`, `review-scope-4b.txt`, `review/verify-4/report.md`, `027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md` and `tasks.md`, `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md`, the eight scope files, `render.ts`, `doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`, `command-offer.mjs`, `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `codex.mjs`.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794681593308,"end":1794681624368}}}}
